\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mixed after Fed cut, wavering yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 02:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 21 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped early Wednesday, finding cold comfort from Wall Street's disappointment over the Federal Reserve's rate cut and the softer yen. \par \par \uc2  However, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were generally long dollars, especially against the Singapore dollar and Korean won. Any turnaround in the yen may convince players to bail out of long dollar positions, giving Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a short-term boost, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Fed cut rates by 50 basis points on Tuesday, bringing the federal funds rate to five percent and the discount rate to 4.5 percent. It also signaled it was ready to take necessary action at any time. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll showed 17 out of 25 primary dealers of U.S. government securities polled after the Fed cut expected another 50 basis point by the next Fed meeting on May 15. For the POLL, double click . \par \par \uc2  But the size of the cut disappointed Wall Street, which had been clamouring for a bigger cut. The technology-laced Nasdaq fell by 4.8 percent, and the Dow Jones Industrial Average lost 2.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  Those falls were expected to pressure tech-senstive equity markets in Taiwan and Korea. \par \par \uc2  On the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the yen saw early gains slip away and the euro managed to rachet up more gains against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was under pressure at around 1.7740, having hit lows of around 1.7760 overnight. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said underpinning the downside was persistent speculation SingTel might drop its bid to buy Australia's Optus . \par \par \uc2  "But until there is clear news here, the market seems unwilling to offload its large U.S. dollar longs," Mansoor Mohi-uddin, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg in Singapore, said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some U.S. investment banks were unwinding long positions, piled up in the run up to March 16 highs of 1.7780. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar has lost 2.5 percent since the beginning of the year, in part because of the weaker yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  That, analysts say, lessened the market concerns about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won opened lower as disappointment over the size of the Fed's rate cut and concerns over the prospect of a U.S. recovery worked through the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  The weaker yen and bearish economic data also weighed on sentiment. Dealers said the won was expected to consolidate in the near term as the market was very long of dollar. \par \par \uc2  "But the dollar's bullish trend is intact. Charts show the dollar/won is still trapped in the uptrend channel which started on February 20," said a dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The market was unnerved by news of Korea's fourth quarter growth shrinking on quarter for the first time since the second quarter of 1998, the nadir of the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said although Korea may avoid technical recession as its economy is likely to grow moderately in the first quarter this year, its gross domestic product might contract again the April-June period. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht dangled just above the 44.00 level as the market continued to favour the dollar despite disappointment over the Fed's rate cut. \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty over the U.S. economy, the weak yen and Thailand's gloomy economic outlook all kept a lid on the baht. \par \par \uc2  "There's not much good news around. The dollar looks a bit overbought and we spotted some profit taking at around 44.00. But I expect dollar bulls to pick it up on dips to 43.80," said a dealer at an Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market's reaction to news that the government would unveil a new fiscal stimulus package in April was muted. \par \par \uc2  "Looking at their fiscal position now, I think there's little room for the government to increase its spending. The delay of value-added tax (VAT) increase would stretch the government's coffer a bit," said a dealer at a foreign bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate was quoted at 6.9/9.9 satang per dollar offshore and -10.50/-10.25 satang onshore. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso eased after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated its desire to follow the Fed rate cut with its own. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said he expected the Monetary Board at its meeting on Thursday to ease key overnight rates by 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  The overnight borrowing rate now stands at 10.5 percent and the lending rate at 12.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut its key rates by 450 basis points after raising them by 400 basis points in October to defend the weak peso . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the peso to trade in a range of 48.50-48.80 with the downside capped by expected dollar inflows from exporters. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was holding above 10,500 in a market wary of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Chief economics minister Rizal Ramli said on Tuesday he had asked the Indonesian bank agency to convert $500 million in asset sales to help the rupiah. He also said he had requested that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  act more decisively to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market, either directly or through state banks. It has also recently raised its benchmark one-month SBI rate to 14.97 percent and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in the rupiah money market by 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was flat in early trade, as the market puzzled over Wall Street's fall, the indecisive yen, and Taiwan's dimming economic prospects. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the U.S. dollar was hugely overbought against the Taiwan dollar, with a reading of around 95 at 0047 GMT. \par \par \uc2  However, sentiment towards Taiwan was still bearish given its dependency on exports to the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, Taiwan will release February export order data and industrial output on Thursday. Recent Reuters polls showed economists on average expected a 10.8 percent on year rise in export orders and a 10.73 percent on year rise in industry output. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0125 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.43\tab  122.94\tab    +0.42\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7750\tab  1.7720\tab    -0.17\par  Taiwan dlr     32.86\tab   32.78\tab    -0.24\par  Korean won   1302.00\tab 1295.90\tab    -0.47\par  Baht\tab      44.07\tab   43.93\tab    -0.32\par  Peso\tab      48.58\tab   47.95\tab    -1.30\par  Rupiah\tab 10420.00     10400.00\tab    -0.19\par  Ringg