\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Lower As Political Woes Continue \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed lower Monday as political and security woes continue to hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at IDR10,430, up from IDR10,325 at Friday's close, but off an intraday high at IDR10,500. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the day, selling a small amount of dollars directly to the market, helping the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recover some ground. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar resistance remains at 10,500," a local trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated the amount of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at about a few million dollars, much less than that of last week. State banks were also selling dollars Monday, probably on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't help lift the rupiah in the longer term, as investors remain concerned over moves to impeach President Abdurrahman Wahid, traders said. The likelihood of further violence also concerns investors, they added. \par \par \uc2  A bomb exploded Saturday on a railway line near Jakarta. There were no casualties but the blast led to more negative sentiment on the market. A wave of bombs in the past twelve months have destabilized the country. \par \par \uc2  Stocks also fell, with the JSX Composite Index closing 3.5% lower, a 28-month low of 367.142 points. \par \par \uc2  Rates fell slightly Monday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to have let the pressure off a tightening cycle, that was aimed at helping the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowed rupiah in the interbank market in an attempt to dry up liquidity and help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise from a 30-month low at 11,500. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be focusing more on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than on rate policy, as interest hikes have very little effect on the politically-driven rupiah at the moment, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank rate closed Monday at 12.75%, down from over 13% earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; tom.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3j0170s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
