\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Indonesia Gov: Will Up Interest Rates If Necessary \b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday through selling dollars, but didn't specify how much it had spent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin told reporters the amount the bank has spent since the start of the rupiah's fall two weeks ago was less than $100 million. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia is also willing to continue raising rates to help the rupiah, which is now trading at 29-month lows to the dollar on political concerns, Sjahril said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been pushing up rates on its one month notes at weekly auction, but this has had little effect on the rupiah given the political nature of its fall, traders say. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Farida Husna, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277;\par farida.husna@dowjones.com\par -0- 19/03/01 09-44G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3j0170p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
