\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Lower On Bleak Political Outlook \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed lower against the U.S. dollar in active dealing Friday, as local companies continued buying the dollar because of the uncertain domestic political situation. \par \par \uc2  After rising to an intraday high of IDR10,375, the dollar closed at IDR10,325, up from its close of IDR10,150 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that local companies bought the dollar in anticipation of foreign debt repayments in two or three months. \par \par \uc2  "Although local companies don't have to repay their foreign debts until the next two or three months, they are buying the dollar now on bleak political outlook," said a dealer with a foreign bank. "Local companies remain skeptical as there are no signs of political truce between President (Abdurrahman Wahid) and his opponents." \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to help the rupiah as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the dollar to foreign banks instead of to local companies, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated Bank Indonesia on Friday sold $40 million in the market, directly and indirectly through state banks and brokers. \par \par \uc2  A statement by senior economic minister Rizal Ramli, that he is optimistic the dollar will fall below IDR10,000 in the near future, failed to calm local companies, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The interbank money market was steady as Bank Indonesia didn't borrow rupiah from the market to tighten liquidity. The overnight rupiah interbank rate was steady between 12.5% - 12.75%. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia usually tightens rupiah liquidity in the interbank money market to reduce the pressure on the rupiah in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  As dollar demand was healthy Friday, dealers expect the dollar to open Monday around IDR10,500, unless Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  promptly. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires;62-21 39831277\par I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com\par -0- 16/03/01 09-59G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3g015q4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
