\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Hunt for value helps regional stocks. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Richard Hubbard \par \uc2 1,101 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 11:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, March 15 (Reuters) - Asian investors searched \par \par \uc2  for value amid the carnage of a U.S.-inspired stock market \par \par \uc2  sell-off on Thursday and found enough to bring many regional \par \par \uc2  bourses off their lows by the close of trading. \par \par \uc2      Surprisingly, it was the tech sector which saw some of the \par \par \uc2  better buying with China Mobile in Hong Kong, \par \par \uc2  Chartered Semiconductor Manufacturing in Singapore \par \par \uc2  and Korea' Samsung SDI Co all posting gains. \par \par \uc2      "For the moment there is value in Asia, it's just that Asia \par \par \uc2  is being hijacked by external events," said Markus Rosgen, \par \par \uc2  Asian equity strategist for ING Barings in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2      "In an outright U.S. recession this region would have a 20 \par \par \uc2  percent downside, but that would make this region very much the \par \par \uc2  cheapest out of the U.S. or Europe," he said. \par \par \uc2      "There is a lot of value out there now, but there's sadly \par \par \uc2  more downside driven by external factors," Rosgen said. \par \par \uc2      Share prices across Asia were hit hard in early trade by \par \par \uc2  Wall St's across the board pummeling overnight amid fears for \par \par \uc2  the health of Japan's banking system. \par \par \uc2      The key Dow Jones Industrial index sank 317.34 points, or \par \par \uc2  3.08 percent, to 9,973.46 -- it was the Dow's 10th-largest \par \par \uc2  point loss ever. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite Index\tab    closed below\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 2,000 mark for the second time this week to end at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,972.10, down 42.68 points or 2.12 percent. The Nasdaq index\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has now shed 60.9 percent from its high of 5,048.62 in March a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par During the Asian day a big turnaround in Tokyo's benchmark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nikkei average emboldened investors in the region to venture\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back and bargain hunt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CHINA PLAYS IN FOCUS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asia's exposure to a U.S. economic slowdown through its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reliance on exports has many players looking to China as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par defensive play because it is one of the few countries with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par robust domestic demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Figures out on Thursday on retail spending showed this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic demand continues strong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     China's retail sales for the January-February period grew\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10.6 percent this year over the same period of 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Since last year the Chinese New Year holiday fell in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par February and this year it was in January, the period covered by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the numbers indicates sales were definitely better.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     China's economy remains on track for seven percent growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this year, according to both official and many private sector\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economists. But export growth has already started to slow down\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and net exports are starting to drag on the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government has pledged to counter the impact of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par external slowdown with increased state infrastructure spending,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while foreign direct investment is streaming into the country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Actual FDI flows were around $40 billion last year and have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been surging during January and February this year - rising 24\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent on year ago levels. If that rate is sustained FDI could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exceed $50 billion this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But analysts say there are still sizeable risks involved in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A risk of policy inertia leading to a slower reform pace\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than the market is expecting is one key factor, according to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chi Lo, Treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Lo said China is under stress on three fronts. On the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic front from the export slowdown; structurally from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continued reform of the state sector; and politically as China\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prepares to pick a new leader in 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There's certainly a heavy amount of optimism over China,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to me this is a strong signal the market may have over-priced\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the pace of Chinese reforms," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SUFFER\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed to enjoy the bounce seen in equity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets as dollar bulls kept up pressure across the region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Concerns over Japan's economic disarray continued to haunt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen with U.S. funds reported to be actively selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local stocks and converting the proceeds into dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers also blamed the weakness in the Indonesian rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  as damping sentiment towards the region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local corporate dollar demand kept the ailing rupiah below\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10,000, despite wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par news Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fined Standard Chartered Bank 9 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah for violating recently installed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  curbs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar had little reprieve in afternoon trading,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sliding to fresh two-and-a-half year lows around 1.7700.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We've been seeing funds out of New York and Europe sold\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Sing dollar moderately to get out of the stock market," a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0950 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.93\tab  119.62\tab    -1.08\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7685\tab  1.7600\tab    -0.48\par  Taiwan dlr     32.53\tab   32.52\tab    -0.03\par  Korean won   1281.70\tab 1277.80\tab    -0.30\par  Baht\tab      43.82\tab   43.54\tab    -0.64\par  Peso\tab      47.93\tab   47.14\tab    -1.65\par  Rupiah\tab  9900.00     10110.00\tab    +2.12\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 