\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Worried by soft yen, regional gloom. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 09:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 15 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to escape the fury of dollar bulls late Thursday with the yen still faint and the regional outlook remaining decisively gloomy. \par \par \uc2  Despite a bounce in downtrodden Tokyo stocks, concerns over Japan's economic disarray continued to haunt the yen . Ratings agency Fitch placed 19 Japanese banks on negative review on Wednesday, sending investors running for dollar cover. \par \par \uc2  U.S. funds were also reported to be scurrying home after another day of heavy losses on Wall Street, driving some regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower as they sold off local stocks and converted the proceeds into dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also blamed the weakness in the Indonesian rupiah as damping sentiment towards the region. Local corporate dollar demand kept the ailing rupiah below 10,000, despite wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after news Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  fined Standard Chartered Bank 9 billion rupiah for violating recently installed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbs. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro remained under pressure, faced with not only its inability to capitalise on woes in Japan and on U.S. equity markets, but also falls on European bourses. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was trapped in a tug-of-war between \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which kept the market cautious, and strong corporate demand for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through two state banks which were estimated to have offered up to $20 million before midday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was also underpinned by news of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fining Standard Chartered Plc's Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  for allegedly breaching tough new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules. \par \par \uc2  "That news and wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lent support to the rupiah. People in the market believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't let the rupiah fall through 10,200," said a dealer at a foreign bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "But at the end of the day, you have genuine strong dollar demand, and genuine concerns over a poorly performing leader who refuses to step down. State companies which the government urged to sell dollars are still net buyers," he said. \par \par \uc2  Before the news of the fine spread in the market, dealers said the dollar looked well-bid after local media reported comments by Finance Minsiter Prijadi Praptosuhardjo that the sale of palm oil plantations to Malaysia's Kumpulan Guthrie was not final. He was reported as saying parliament should have been consulted. \par \par \uc2  Expectations that IBRA would convert some $345 million in the market from that sale had helped support the rupiah on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso lurched lower but was still trapped in its recent range, weighed by weak regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar demand from a state utilities company, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was wedged in a 48.33-48.49 range. Trading volume was relatively brisk, with around $148.50 million traded compared with $66 million on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "One state company has been in the market since yesterday to buy the dollar to service debt. The amount was quite big relative to the turnover," said a dealer at a European bank in Manila. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its key overnight rates unchanged at 10.5 percent for the borrowing rate and 12.75 percent for the lending rate. \par \par \uc2  The bank has cut rates by 450 basis points since December after raising them by 400 basis points in October to defend the peso in the face of a political crisis. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar had little reprieve in afternoon trading, sliding to fresh two-and-a-half year lows around 1.7700. \par \par \uc2  "We've been seeing funds out of New York and Europe sold the Sing dollar moderately to get out of the stock market," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Straits Times Index was off its worst but still near its lowest level since April 1999, having lost around nine percent since the beginning of the month. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the flow of funds and bleak outlook for the yen pointed to a weak Sing dollar, but fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore would slow its decline. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht sank to its lowest level since January 2 as corporate and interbank players continued to buy the dollar in the wake of a weak yen, despite high baht funding costs offshore. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said one hedge fund had been asking around for prices, but it was not clear if it took any positions against the baht. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said on Thursday the baht was not depreciating too quickly. His remark was interpreted by the market as implying the bank was not disturbed by the baht's recent losses and would let it fall further. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol also said that one bank had been barred from participating in the local repo market - where financial institutions get cheap funds - for 10 days after it breached \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said Thailand was unlikely to face another economic crisis and fresh baht instability. But his remark failed to stop the market from selling the baht. \par \par \uc2  The one-month forward rate in the offshore market eased to 6/11 satang per dollar from 10/12 satang earlier, but was still high compared to last week's range. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar fell under the weight of the soggy yen, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped it off its lows. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted selling U.S. dollars around the high of 32.615. \par \par \uc2  Local banks in Taipei quickly followed suit, helping bring the Taiwan dollar back to 32.55. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. dollar remained well-bid on the offshore non-deliverable forward market, with the one-month at 0.125/140 at 0826 GMT against 0.10/13 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  "Investors are taking long dollar positions in the NDFs because the fundamentals for Taiwan are expected to weaken," said a dealer at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan relies heavily on its high-tech exports and is now faced with a limping technology sector, a slowdown in its largest export market - the U.S. - and a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for one of its biggest competitors - Japan. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was off its lows but still weak after hitting a near two-month trough of 1,290 per dollar on the back of the sagging yen and early losses in Korean stocks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said further falls were contained by exporter dollar sales and fears of government efforts to limit the won's slide, as was the case when it hit 25-month lows of 1,293 in January. \par \par \uc2  Bargain-hunting in Korean stocks also cushioned the won somewhat, but with foreign investors selling a hefty 55 billion won worth of local shares, dealers expected it to remain weighed. \par \par \uc2  Labour Minister Kim Ho-jin estimated the unemployment rate for February would be five percent or 1.069 million people, but he expected the number of jobless to fall to 980,000-990,000 in March. February data is due next week. \par \par \uc2  Korea's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate was 4.1 percent in January and 3.9 percent in December. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0844 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.83\tab  119.62\tab    -1.00\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7665\tab  1.7600\tab    -0.37\par  Taiwan dlr    32.555\tab  32.520\tab    -0.11\par  Korean won   1281.70\tab 1277.80\tab    -0.30\par  Baht\tab      43.85\tab   43.54\tab    -0.71\par  Peso\tab      47.93\tab   47.14\tab    -1.65\par  Rupiah\tab 10020.00     10110.00\tab    +0.90\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.83\tab  114.45\tab    -5.28\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7665\tab  1.7365\tab    -1.70\par  Taiwan dlr    32.555\tab  32.900\tab    +1.06\par  Korean won   1281.70\tab 1277.00\tab    -0.37\par  Baht\tab      43.85\tab   43.70\tab    -0.34\par  Peso\tab      47.93\tab   50.75\tab    +5.88\par  Rupiah\tab 10020.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -5.49\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3f03v3h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760