\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Up On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , But Drop Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed higher Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but traders said the trend remains bullish for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 10,200 rupiah, down from IDR10,500 at Monday's finish. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $70 million for rupiah in the market, helping to buoy the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is at 29-month lows on political concerns. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia also asked commercial banks for prices to borrow money in the interbank market in a bid to dry up rupiah liquidity, which would also help the unit. \par \par \uc2  Interbank overnight rates rushed up to 30% amid expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would accept high rates to help the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  In the event, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  canceled its plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the money market, saying the offered rates were too high. At the close, the overnight interbank rate was back where it started the day at 12.5%. \par \par \uc2  Both dollar selling from gross \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of $29 billion and raising rates are unlikely to help the rupiah in the long-term, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Investors are still dollar hungry amid the current political situation, which looks likely to topple President Abdurrahman Wahid in the near future. \par \par \uc2  "The political situation hasn't changed," said a trader at a Jakarta-based foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  "Investors are just waiting until Bank Indonesia stops selling dollars then they will buy dollars again." \par \par \uc2  Resistance for the dollar Wednesday is set at IDR10,600, its intraday high Tuesday. Strong support is seen at IDR10,000. \par \par \uc2  Only capital controls, which would likely set the dollar at a much lower rate, would lead to a sustained rise in the rupiah, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The government, which has committed to a floating exchange rate under its International Monetary Fund program, has ruled out imposing capital controls. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277\par tom.wright@dowjones.com\par -0- 13/03/01 09-18G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3d015e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
