\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Pulling Dlr Back To IDR10,375 \b0\par\par\uc2 146 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 03:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah early Tuesday, selling around $20 million through brokers, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia sold around $50 million Monday to help the rupiah, which is now trading at 29-month lows to the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't lead to a sustained rally in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is down on political concerns. \par \par \uc2  Thousands of students called for President Abdurrahman Wahid to resign Monday, circling his palace in downtown Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  The president is facing likely impeachment by parliament for connection with two financial scandals. Wahid is also under fire for failure to stamp out a recent wave of ethnic violence. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277;\par tom.wright@dowjones.com\par -0- 13/03/01 02-39G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3d014l1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
