\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Indonesia says will continue helping rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2 162 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 07:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, March 12 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would continue to do its best, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to defend the fast-sliding rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to do its best," deputy governor Miranda Goeltom told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "We have enough funds to help the rupiah... we will continue to do it (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has fallen around 10 percent from late Friday levels, though by 0627 GMT had recovered some ground and was quoted at 10,400/10,500 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Goeltom said she expected rates to rise at Wednesday's auction of short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paper (SBIs) and said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate in the money market by 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, senior deputy bank governor Anwar Nasution called \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at the moment like pouring water into the sand, saying an end to political instability was crucial to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3c04473\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
