\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Gloom here, there, everywhere. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Jennifer Chen \par \uc2 968 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 09:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 12 (Reuters) - Asian equity and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  markets sank on Monday, overwhelmed by bad news from Wall \par \par \uc2  Street and Japan. \par \par \uc2      On top of that, Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar, were contending with a flailing Indonesian \par \par \uc2  rupiah , which skidded to lows not seen since September \par \par \uc2  1998. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The U.S. Nasdaq\tab    market fell victim on Friday to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors whose hopes of a deep rate cut from the Federal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reserve were dashed by positive February jobs data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Nasdaq's 5.35 percent fall, chip giant Intel Corp's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  profit warning, and bad news from other U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par technology leaders like Cisco sent Asian tech stocks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reeling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Tech-sensitive bourses in Singapore\tab  , Taiwan\tab   ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and Korea all stumbled over the losses on Nasdaq.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Benchmark indices in Tokyo and Hong Kong\tab   fell back\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as well, with Japan's Nikkei faced with a home-grown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par brew of economic and political troubles.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     STUMBLING YEN, MIXED-UP GOVERNMEMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Prime Minister Yoshiro Mori's decision over the weekend to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par push the elections of his party's president ahead of schedule\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seemed to clear Japan's murky political scene.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But his denial on Monday that he intended to resign muddied\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par those waters even more.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite slightly better than expected October-December\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic growth data, the market remained deeply pessimistic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over Japan's prospects.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts shrugged off the 0.8 percent rise in gross\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic product, saying most indicators still pointed down.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Those concerns, questions over the country's leadership,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par scepticism over the ruling coalition's economic package and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nasdaq's fall pushed the Nikkei to a 16-year closing low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab   fell below 120, casting a shadow over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets that have been under its thumb in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "At this point, we're certainly seeing that regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness...under the shadow of the yen," said Song Sen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wun, vice president of regional economics at G.K. Goh Research\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     With sickly markets in Japan and the United States, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par euro was looking quite hale in comparison.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SUFFERING RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, the yen's woes paled next to the rupiah's. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crashed to a low of 11,210 -- its worst\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since September 22, 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah managed to claw back from that following verbal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Dealers in Jakarta\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said the bank offered between $5-$10 million in the afternoon,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after it offered $2 million in the morning to no avail.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's economic and political woes sideswiped the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah earlier in the day as nervous interbank players bid up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar for fear of the situation getting worse.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Among the chief concerns in the market were those centred\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Jakarta's frayed relationship with the International\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monetary Fund and the leadership of embattled President\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Abdurrahman Wahid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par News of protests in Jakarta by pro-and anti-Wahid factions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pushed the market over the edge, as investors fretted over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible violence between the two sides.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A straw poll of analysts surveyed by Reuters on Monday said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that barring capital controls and a significant turnaround in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the political situation, the rupiah could hit 12,000-15,000 by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the end of June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The two things that I'm looking at are the situation with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the IMF and the situation with Wahid... Even if things are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par patched up with the IMF, things still will look shaky if Wahid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hasn't stepped down by June," said an analyst at a foreign bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The IMF has delayed since December a $400 million loan to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jakarta over concerns about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  independence, regional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par autonomy and asset sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "While the loan itself isn't a lot, it means a lot as far\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as investor confidence," said Nizam Idris, regional economist\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at IDEAglobal.com in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wahid said on Monday he would not resign, and called upon\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hugely popular Vice President Megawati Sukarnoputri to become\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more proactive.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0817 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.38\tab  119.62\tab    -0.63\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7608\tab  1.7560\tab    -0.27\par  Taiwan dlr     32.47\tab   32.40\tab    -0.22\par  Korean won   1277.20\tab 1269.00\tab    -0.64\par  Baht\tab      43.68\tab   43.53\tab    -0.34\par  Peso\tab      48.00\tab   48.00\tab    +0.00\par  Rupiah\tab 10400.00\tab 9975.00\tab    -4.09\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.38\tab  114.45\tab    -4.93\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7608\ta