\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Depressed by yen, rupiah wretched. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 09:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 12 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  started the the week on a glum note as doubts over the leadership in Japan and Indonesia came to a head, battering the yen and the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell past 11,000 for the first time since September 24, 1998 as companies and banks rushed to buy dollars amid mounting concern about the political and economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  Analysts predicted it could slide further, barring capital controls or a significant improvement in the political situation. \par \par \uc2  "If the rupiah continues to go at its current pace, I think the government would come up with fresh measures...ie, one form of capital control or another. In that case, it could pick up to around 10,000," said Andrew Fung, head of Asia Pacific treasury research at Rabobank. \par \par \uc2  "Barring that, there is a possibility that it could go to 13,000. I still think the rupiah should trade above 10,000, but sentiment is driving market dynamics at this point," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht traded at the lower end of its recent range as good news on the national asset management company, soon to be established to tackle non-performing loans, was clouded by the yen and the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar slipped past 1.7600 which had been expected to be the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threshold, sparking speculation it could test 1.7650. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar trailed off to three-and-a-half month lows of 1.7620 to the dollar on relatively healthy turnover. \par \par \uc2  Weakness mainly owed to the Indonesian rupiah, which tends to move the Sing dollar when it moves sharply. Singapore and Indonesia have traditionally had close investment ties. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the lagging stock market following the Nasdaq sell-off and the weaker yen dampened sentiment. They added that Sing dollar selling partly owed to talk of Singapore Telecommunications making a bigger-than-expected bid for Cable and Wireless Optus . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing dollar was unlikely to fall much beyond 1.7620, a low last seen in late November, due to jitters over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso trimmed losses to end at around 48.07 per dollar, having fallen to around 48.25 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  "That was a knee-jerk reaction to the falling rupiah and the yen. But the sell-off didn't last because we have a relatively stable economy and now the political situation is better off," a trader at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  He added the peso should settle into a snug range of 47.00 to 48.50 in the short term. \par \par \uc2  "We need to see a firmer stock market, more offshore demand and more foreign investment for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to break the range trading," he added. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won continued to be weighed by weakness in the yen and declines in local stocks, gapping down at the open and hitting a an early low of 1,280.1. \par \par \uc2  Exporter and state bank dollar sales near that level kept it from falling any further but dealers expected limited upside as foreign investors remained net sellers of Korean equities for the third straight session. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark KOSPI ended 3.66 percent lower as foreigners unloaded tech shares following the Nasdaq's 5.35 percent drop on Friday. Bank shares were also sold on disappointment with a decision by Korean creditors to support the cash-starved Hyundai Group. Data released on Monday offered little cause for cheer, with the current account surplus almost halving on the month in January to a provisional $684.4 million. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the faltering semiconductor sector, a main export segment, would keep pressure on the economy. \par \par \uc2  J.P. Morgan said it would cut its 2001 growth forecast for Korea to 3.5 percent or lower from four percent as weakness in the electronics sector remained a concern despite improvements in consumer and business sentiment and industrial output. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah hit a 30-month trough, before verbal and actual dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted a bounce. \par \par \uc2  Mounting concerns about the government's inability to contain ethnic violence and revive the economy, and the fate of IMF loans spurred dollar demand from banks and local companies in a thin market. \par \par \uc2  News of the closure of three gas fields by Exxon Mobil Oil Indonesia in northern Aceh on Friday due to security concerns added to the gloom as the Indonesian economy relies heavily on oil and gas exports. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah extended losses after deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Anwar Nasution said BI had limited ability to defend it. \par \par \uc2  That remark was later countered by another BI deputy governor who said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and had adequate reserves to do so. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said BI backed its comments with actual dollar sales worth around $5-$10 million, causing the rupiah to bounce above the 11,000 level. \par \par \uc2  "It's almost a one-way market. Bank Indonesia and state banks were among few dollar providers. Exporters are not selling," said a Jakarta dealer. \par \par \uc2  "If it goes on like this, I bet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do something. I don't think it will be a capital control. They might be looking into ways to force exporters to bring in dollar revenues," he said. \par \par \uc2  Chief economics minister Rizal Ramli said 8,000 was an acceptable level for the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was wedged in a narrow 43.55-43.75 range. Investors were reluctant to take profits on the dollar due to gloom in the rupiah and the yen, but they were not willing to build on their already long dollar positions either. \par \par \uc2  The market welcomed news that the soon-to-be-established national asset management company would buy up to 250 billion baht ($5.74 million) of bad loans from private banks at book value net of loan loss reserves. \par \par \uc2  It had earlier said it might absorb as little as 120 billion baht at discounts. \par \par \uc2  "The news seems to be benefitting bank and finance shares more than the baht. I guess people will be watching how efficient and transparent the AMC is and the rate of loan recovery," said a dealer at a European bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  "The baht didn't move much today. The market is already pretty long of the dollar, but at the same time there is no compelling reason to buy the baht either," he said. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs offshore nudged up, with the one-month forward rate rising to 1.5/2.5 satang per dollar. TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar slid to its lowest level since January 30, edging closer to 32.50 per dollar on declines in local stocks and a depressed yen. \par \par \uc2  The market was keen to test its downside after Friday's close below 32.40, which prompted speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had moved its line of defence back to 32.50. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan shares ended lower for the third straight session as heavyweight electronics shares were hurt by the Nasdaq's drop. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0855 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.38\tab  119.62\tab    -0.63\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7595\tab  1.7560\tab    -0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    32.473\tab  32.402\tab    -0.22\par  Korean won   1270.00\tab 1269.10\tab    -0.07\par  Baht\tab      43.66\tab   43.53\tab    -0.30\par  Peso\tab      48.13\tab   48.00\tab    -0.27\par  Rupiah\tab 10200.00\tab 9975.00\tab    -2.21\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.38\tab  114.45\tab    -4.93\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7595\tab  1.7365\tab    -1.31\par  Taiwan dlr    32.473\tab  32.900\tab    +1.31\par  Korean won   1270.00\tab 1277.00\tab    +0.55\par  Baht\tab      43.66\tab   43.70\tab    +0.09\par  Peso\tab      48.13\tab   50.75\tab    +5.44\par  Rupiah\tab 10200.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -7.16\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3c0423m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
