\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Rupiah bounces as Bank Indonesia steps in. \b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 08:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 12 (Reuters) - The bruised rupiah clawed back above the 11,000 mark as players rushed to unload the dollar after Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in with verbal and actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah bounced to 10,500 from around 11,200 just minutes after Bank Indonesia senior deputy governor Miranda Goeltom said the bank would do its best to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Bank Indonesia will continue to do its best. We have enough funds to help the rupiah ... we will continue to do it (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," Goeltom told Reuters in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered between $5-$10 million in the market in the afternoon after selling around $2 million to no avail in the morning. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah floundered past 11,200 per dollar earlier on Monday on mounting concerns over Indonesia's political and economic woes, with analysts predicting a further drop. \par \par \uc2  Goeltom's remark contradicted earlier comments by deputy governor Anwar Nasution who said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had limited ability to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . His statement sent the rupiah reeling to its worst level since September 24, 1998. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said doubts over President Abdurrahman Wahid's leadership and his ability to handle economic and ethnic problems had spurred dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  News that thousands of anti and pro-government protesters had poured on to the streets of Jakarta also unnerved the market. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia and state banks were the only sellers of dollars in a thin market as most exporters held on to their dollar earnings and Indonesian companies and banks sold rupiah. \par \par \uc2  MORE DECLINES \par \par \uc2  In a straw poll on Monday, most analysts surveyed by Reuters said barring capital controls and a significant turnaround in the political situation, the rupiah could head toward 12,000-15,000 by the end of June. \par \par \uc2  "If the rupiah continues to go at its current pace, I think the government would come up with fresh measures ... i.e. one form of capital control or another. In that case, it could pick up to around 10,000," said Andrew Fung, head of Asia-Pacific treasury research at Rabobank. \par \par \uc2  "Barring that, there is a possibility that it could go to 13,000. I still think the rupiah should trade above 10,000, but sentiment is driving market dynamics at this point," he said. \par \par \uc2  Another analyst at a foreign bank in Singapore said if things continued as they were, the rupiah could falter to anywhere between 12,500-15,000. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit an all-time low of about 17,000 in June, 1998. \par \par \uc2  "The two things that I'm looking at are the situation with the IMF and the situation with Wahid ... Even if things are patched up with the IMF, things still will look shaky if Wahid hasn't stepped down by June," the analyst said. \par \par \uc2  Most analysts believe the IMF will not pull out of Indonesia and is soon likely to disburse long-delayed loan payments. \par \par \uc2  But they expected the Fund to stick to its guns on the four key issues related to the sale of state shares in two major banks, amendments to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, borrowing by regions and corporate debt restructuring. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3c041no\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
