\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah Up To 10,500/Dlr On Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 07:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in thin lunchtime trade Monday, helping to pull the rupiah back from 30-month lows, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia sold around a $5 million while most traders were at lunch, adding to a similar amount of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning. \par \par \uc2  The dollar selling pushed the rupiah back to IDR10,500 versus a IDR11,500 high in morning trade on political concerns. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to lead to a sustained rally in the rupiah, which remains under pressure as thousands of student protesters Monday call for President Abdurrahman Wahid to resign. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Anwar Nasution admitted that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to help support the rupiah, and urged politicians to stop bickering. \par \par \uc2  Many lawmakers want Wahid to resign, and blame him for the country's myriad of economic and social problems. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; tom.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3c013vj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
