\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore MAS Reaffirms Modest, Gradual SGD Rise Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's policy stance of a gradual and modest appreciation of the Singapore dollar remains unchanged, a spokeswoman told Dow Jones Newswires Monday. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply Monday, mirroring the fall of the Indonesian rupiah and the yen. Around 0942 GMT (4:42 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7617, up from S$1.7571 late Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rose to an intraday high of S$1.7622 - its highest since November last year - as the Indonesian and Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell amid growing political uncertainty in Indonesia and Japan. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman also declined to offer specific comments on the level of the Singapore dollar Monday. \par \par \uc2  With the MAS making no effort to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , banks, investors and local companies continued to buy U.S. dollars at levels above S$1.7610 even after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell below IDR11,000 on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and retreated from its high against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In a move that surprised most analysts, the MAS in February affirmed its policy of allowing a "gradual, modest appreciation" of the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The MAS manages the Singapore dollar exchange rate against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the country's major trading partners and competitors. It maintains the trade-weighted exchange rate within an undisclosed band. \par \par \uc2  -By Hasan Jafri, Dow Jones Newswires; 65/421-4828; hasan.jafri@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3c012ok\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
