\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah flounders as others stand firm. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 9 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah slammed into 29-month lows on Friday, while other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were tethered to a steadier yen. \par \par \uc2  But their prospects were not looking very sunny, as the yen stumbled over the Japanese government's emergency economic package in late Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  Local corporate demand for dollars finally pushed the rupiah over the 10,000 mark, which it last saw on October 7, 1998, according to Reuters Graphics data. \par \par \uc2  Direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar selling by state banks failed to bolster the rupiah. Heavily indebted Indonesian companies have been snapping up dollars in recent sessions as the first quarter end nears and amid the country's deepening political and economic crisis. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  enjoyed a reprieve for most of the session as yen bears took a break ahead of the announcement of the emergency economic package. \par \par \uc2  The yen has suffered this week at the hands of a market confused by sometimes conflicting statements from various government officials. \par \par \uc2  Its stuttering movements have dominated activity in regional markets, and left most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in weaker ranges. \par \par \uc2  With the yen very much in the hot seat, the euro was steady, helped by the relatively brighter outlook for Europe's economy compared with the U.S. and Japan's. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah dropped past 10,000, succumbing to mounting pressure from local corporate demand for dollars despite Bank Indonesia's efforts to rein it in. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  later said direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "standard procedure," adding that the bank had enough reserves to defend the rupiah and there was no need to impose capital controls. \par \par \uc2  However, a prominent local banker called on the government to force Indonesian exporters to repatriate their earnings. Gunarni Soewaoro, the head of the local bank association Perbanas, said such an idea would be more palatable given the gridlock between Indonesia and its chief donor the IMF. \par \par \uc2  Local companies who are seeking to fulfil dollar requirements by the end of the first quarter have fueled the dollar buying spree, as the market remained on edge over Indonesia's economic and political woes. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the main concern was the stalled talks between the IMF and Jakarta, which have helding up a $400 million loan disbursement. Jakarta said on Friday it hoped to resolve its differences with the IMF this month. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 The won gained as the firmer yen spurred unwinding of long dollar positions, but dealers dismissed it as merely a short-term reprieve given persistent worries about Japan's outlook. \par \par \uc2  Further foreign fund sales of local shares also limited the won's upside prospects, but dealers said a reluctance to take aggressive positions before the release of U.S. jobs data later in the day dampened overall trading interest. \par \par \uc2  The won was expected to face near term resistance around 1,260, which marks the 38 percent retracement of the dollar's February 21-March 8 rise. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht shifted to the middle of its recent range of around 43.30-43.70 as the market rooted around for fresh factors. \par \par \uc2  For the past several sessions, the baht has been caught tracking the yen's moves. But with little activity in the yen for most of the session, the baht was stuck in a holding pattern. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Bangkok and Singapore said activity was dull amid a general feeling the market was long of dollars. \par \par \uc2  However, many players were still reluctant to unwind their long dollar positions, hoping for another push towards 43.70 if the yen should fall past 120 again. \par \par \uc2  The government had yet to announce the pricing formula for its planned asset managememt company. Government officials and bankers were meeting to discuss details of the plan. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's finance minsitry also said it would issue 94 billion baht worth of government and Financial Institutions Development Fund bonds between April and June, and 20 billion baht worth of savings bonds, to help plug the budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso weakened slightly in a somewhat delayed reaction to the unsteadiness of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said trading was uneventful with dollar sales from local exporters quickly matched by bids from interbank players mindful of a dimming peso outlook. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, dealers said they were bracing for the local import season, which starts in April. They added the sagging sentiment towards regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the midst of the global economic slowdown did not bode well for the peso. \par \par \uc2  However, French-based investment bank BNP Paribas said on Friday it felt the impact of the U.S. economic slowdown on Asia was overstated, and predicted the Philippines would weather the downturn well. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was off its low as fears of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted some players to sell the U.S. dollar near 1.7600. \par \par \uc2  The troubled rupiah and expectations of high demand for the dollar in the wake of fresh mergers and acquisition activity should continue to weigh on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "People in the market believe the Singtel and Optus deal is a done deal. But I think the company must have covered most if not all of its dollar demand to buy Optus," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "News of PSA aiming to buy a Belgian company also added to the downward pressure," he said. \par \par \uc2  Singapore port operator PSA Corp said on Friday it intended to buy at least 51 percent of Hesse Noord Natie (HNN), a newly merged Belgian port management company. \par \par \uc2  HNN has been valued at between 580 million and 650 million euros ($541 million and $606 million). \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar ended easier, slipping past the 32.40 per dollar level as local shares slipped for the second day and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market fretted over the yen's dim outlook. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark TAIEX was hit by sales of heavyweight tech stocks after the Nasdaq's 2.48 percent fall and Intel's third straight sales warning. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift the Taiwan dollar off early lows of 32.418, but they expected a range of 32.40-32.50 for next week. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0914 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.54\tab  119.60\tab    +0.05\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7566\tab  1.7567\tab    +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    32.402\tab  32.381\tab    -0.06\par  Korean won   1268.80\tab 1270.00\tab    +0.09\par  Baht\tab    