\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Indonesia rupiah hits 29-month low. \b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 08:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 9 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah hit 29-month lows on Friday as local companies sought dollars for debt servicing needs amid growing gloom about the country's political and economic picture. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said the rupiah traded at a low of 10,040 to the dollar in late afternoon trade shortly after hitting 10,000 for the first time since October 7, 1998, according to Reuters Graphics data. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said state banks were seen selling dollars in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets all morning as the rupiah extended its slide. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly early in the day, selling an estimated $20 million at 9,920/30, they said. \par \par \uc2  BANK \b \highlight22\uc2 INDONESIA INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin later said direct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "standard procedure". \par \par \uc2  He said the bank had enough reserves to defend the rupiah and that there was no need to impose capital controls. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's gross foreign reserves stood at $29.09 billion as of February 19, down from $29.11 billion the previous week. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's defence, dealers in Jakarta said the rupiah could slip further. "If the demand is still there, we could touch 10,050," said a dealer at a foreign bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, the offshore rupiah non-deliverable forward market was anxiously monitoring the spot market. \par \par \uc2  "It's not good that 10,000 was broken without much of a fight," said an NDF dealer at a foreign bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  At 0659 GMT, the one-month rupiah NDF was quoted by Prebon Yamane at 10,400/10,500. The six-month was at 11,400/11,600. \par \par \uc2  GLOOM GROWS \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has come under growing pressure recently as heavily indebted companies buy dollars to make end-quarter payments on foreign loans. \par \par \uc2  Mounting pessimism about President Abdurrahman Wahid's shaky leadership and a long-running spat with the International Monetary Fund, which could jeopardise a $5.8 billion debt rescheduling deal with the Paris Club of official creditors, have also weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The IMF delayed a $400 million loan to Indonesia in December, amid concerns about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence and worries that new regional autonomy laws would lead to fiscal laxity. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, a prominent Indonesian banker urged the government to force exporters to repatriate their earnings. \par \par \uc2  "There has to be...(forced export earnings repatriation) to help the economy," Gunarni Soeworo, head of the local influential association of local banks Perbanas, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "Under normal conditions there is no need to do so, but we cannot expect this to happen (voluntarily) in the current situation," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx390465g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
