\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah hits 10,000/dlr, 29-month low. \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 05:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 9 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah hit a 29-month low of 10,000 per dollar on Friday as local companies sought dollars for debt servicing needs amid growing gloom about the political and economic picture. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said it slid to 10,000, the first time it had touched that level since October 7, 1998, according to Reuters Graphics data. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said state banks had been spotted selling dollars in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets all morning as the rupiah extended its slide. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly early in the day, selling an estimated $20 million at 9,920/30 rupiah, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has come under growing pressure as heavily indebted local companies buy dollars to make end-quarter payments on foreign loans. \par \par \uc2  Mounting pessimism about President Abdurrahman Wahid's shaky leadership and a long-running spat with the International Monetary Fund, which could jeopardise a $5.8 billion debt rescheduling deal with the Paris Club of official creditors, have also weighed. \par \par \uc2  The IMF delayed a $400 million loan to Indonesia in December due to concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence and regional autonomy laws. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx39045k2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
