\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends At 29-Mo Low On Politics, \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah plunged to a 29-month low Friday as rising domestic political conflicts and moves by international ratings agencies continued to fuel dollar buying, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Standard & Poor's Thursday cut its outlook on the country's sovereign debt to negative from stable. Earlier in the week Moody's Investors Service cut its outlook on Indonesia's sovereign rating to stable from positive. The cuts confirmed the market's already bearish sentiment on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Despite Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , amid strong demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar easily broke through the psychologically important level of IDR10,000 Friday. After rising to IDR10,140, the dollar ended at IDR10,090 compared to its close at IDR9,930 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank Indonesia likely spent around $60 million Friday to defend the rupiah - directly and through indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by state banks. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's rise seemed to be unstoppable as everyone was buying the dollar," said a dealer with a local bank. "People were worried that the political conflict has reached the grass-root level." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market ignored Bank Indonesia Governor Sjahril Sabirin's warning that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "With gross \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve of around $29 billion, the market knows that Bank Indonesia's pockets aren't deep," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's sharp increase pushed the one-month interbank money market rate higher to 15.25%, from less than 14% Thursday, as banks borrowed rupiah in the money market to back their dollar-long positions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The one-month swap premium increased to 25% from around 20% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's plunge also dragged Indonesian share prices 3.3% lower Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise to above IDR10,000 is expected to trigger further dollar buying next week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's rise may incite panic dollar buying in the society like what happened in mid-1998, when many Indonesian bought dollars as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis was escalating into political crisis. "IDR10,000 is a very important psychological level," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to test the next resistance level of IDR10,500 Monday before rising to IDR11,000 if Bank Indonesia fails to increase its dollar selling. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana,Dow Jones Newswires;62-21 39831277 I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx39011bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
