\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Flat;Off Lows On State Bk Dlr Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed unchanged Friday, but off earlier lows amid state bank dollar selling, likely on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market earlier Friday saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sell dollars if necessary to help the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  In late trade, traders observed state banks selling dollars, which pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from day highs at IDR9,890 to finish trade in Asia unchanged from Thursday's close at IDR9,860. \par \par \uc2  At these levels the rupiah is at its lowest point since October 1998. \par \par \uc2  The dollar climbed to its highs earlier in the day amid investor concerns over the shaky political situation, and continued ethnic violence across the archipelago. \par \par \uc2  With President Abdurrahman Wahid still under attack from Parliament the dollar will likely test IDR9,910 resistance next week. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's onshore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is closed Monday for a national public holiday, but it will reopen Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Offshore investors took long dollar positions through the non-deliverable rupiah forward market Friday to hedge against the political situation. \par \par \uc2  The NDF market is an attempt by offshore banks to get round new Bank Indonesia rules that basically ban offshore trading in the rupiah. As the NDF market settles contracts in dollars it doesn't need any rupiah supply. \par \par \uc2  Onshore market players took their cue from the NDF market, selling rupiah on the spot market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Governor Sjahril said the rupiah's recent fall to more than two-year lows was due to politics, but he added the dollar would have gone above IDR10,000 if it hadn't been for the new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules which have reduced speculation in he rupiah. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277\par tom.wright@dowjones.com\par -0- 02/03/01 09-38G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3200xsu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
