\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Clouded by yen, Greenspan eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,172 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2001\par 10:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 28 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated in late trade on Wednesday as the dollar rose after the Bank of Japan cut interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ trimmed the overnight call rate and official discount rate by 10 basis points to 0.15 percent and 0.25 percent respectively, citing slowing overseas growth and declining stock prices. \par \par \uc2  The news caused the yen to drop briefly to around 116.70 from about 116 before the announcement. \par \par \uc2  The overall mood was cautious after Tuesday's news of a sharp drop in U.S. consumer confidence and ahead of Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's congressional testimony at 1430 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think Greenspan would want to sound unduly pessimistic, especially coming just 14 days after his recent testimony," said Lee Boon Keng, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at DBS. \par \par \uc2  "So, I think we will get another rate cut in the next meeting. Those who expect an inter-meeting cut might be in for disappointment," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah remained soggy despite support from state banks as local corporate demand for dollars lurked against the backdrop of political troubles and an unresolved row between the IMF and the government. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht slipped as the market digested dismal trade numbers showing a deficit in January - the second in 40 months. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah managed to hold to a firmer footing as state banks sold dollars in its defense. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and and might hike interest rates to boost the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The key one-month SBI rate edged up to 14.79 percent from 14.75 percent at last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction, below the 10-15 basis point rise expected by analysts. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said state banks sold dollars around the day's high of 9,632. But the rupiah still faced the tricky mix of poor sentiment and local corporate demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Another potential prop for the rupiah was also removed, with the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA) saying it was delaying the conversion of $500 million into rupiah "for various reasons". IBRA had previously said it planned to convert the money from mid-February in conjunction with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah, which has weakened over two percent since the beginning of the year, slipped to a 29-month low of 9,910 on Tuesday as already depressed sentiment took a turn for the worse amid worsening ethnic violence in Borneo. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht hovered near 43.00, but was off its intraday low as late news of a current account surplus offered some relief after the disappointing trade data. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Bangkok said some interbank players took profits on the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released current account and foreign debt data. \par \par \uc2  The current account showed a $298 million surplus in January despite a trade deficit of $282 million in the same month. Total private sector foreign debt fell to $46.4 billion at end-December against $47.2 billion the previous month. \par \par \uc2  The market was cautious ahead of stricter \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  disclosure rules to take effect on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "It could affect trading volume in the market. But again, it might not be as bad as most people think it will be. We'll see," said a dealer at a local bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was stuck at the weaker end of a narrow 48.20-48.335 range as the market unwound long peso positions following its failure to reach highs of 45-46 despite a better political scene. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said the market was reluctant to take new positions ahead of a pending Supreme Court decision on former President Joseph Estrada's petition to be declared the legitimate president. Court officials said on Tuesday the decision would be made in around 10 days. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Bureau of Treasury officials said on Wednesday they would continue to offer some Treasury bonds over the counter to meet immediate funding needs. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury announced on Monday it would suspend auctions of new bond issues for at least a month to reduce borrowing costs. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was unmoved on Wednesday, with the Taipei spot market closed for a national holiday and offshore dealers of non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) reluctant to make bids. \par \par \uc2  But NDF dealers in Singapore said they expected pressure on spot and forward rates when trading resumes on Thursday, citing a 4.36 percent fall in the Nasdaq overnight and a weaker yen after the BOJ's rate cut. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar is vulnerable to shifts in the tech-heavy Nasdaq through foreign investment in stocks, and to the yen's moves as Taiwan competes with Japan in key exports to the U.S. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won closed slightly lower, pressured by a weaker yen, and the Nasdaq's dour performance, but losses were trimmed by month-end dollar offers from exporters. \par \par \uc2  It ended at 1,250.8 per dollar, near its opening of 1,250.7. It had closed Tuesday at 1,246.5. \par \par \uc2  Trade was driven by position-squaring ahead of Greenspan's testimony and a Korean holiday on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "For the time being, the dollar looks set to continue trading in a 1,245-1,255 range with a breakout most likely to come from further deteriorating U.S. data or from the falling Nasdaq," said a UBS Warburg report. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was hovering near the weaker end of its subdued intra-day 1.7400-1.7430 range after spiking higher overnight on stop-loss dollar sales in thin London trade. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/Sing rose briefly to 1.7430 on Wednesday before profit-taking set in as the yen came off its initial rate cut-inspired lows. \par \par \uc2  "It was just the market getting spooked," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  But other dealers said players were selling dollars in expectation of a cut before the Fed's next rate-setting meeting on March 20. \par \par \uc2  "I think 1.7390 is a bargain for dollars at this point," a dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0907 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.48\tab  116.13\tab    -0.30\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7417\tab  1.7407\tab    -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    32.343\tab  32.345\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1251.50\tab 1248.50\tab    -0.24\par  Baht\tab      42.94\tab   42.82\tab    -0.28\par  Peso\tab      48.25\tab   48.18\tab    -0.15\par  Rupiah\tab  9825.00\tab 9840.00\tab    +0.15\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.48\tab  114.45\tab    -1.74\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7417\tab  1.7365\tab    -0.30\par  Taiwan dlr    32.343\tab  32.900\tab    +1.72\par  Korean won   1251.50\tab 1277.00\tab    +2.04\par  Baht\tab      4