\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Rangebound ahead of Greenspan. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2001\par 09:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 27 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dragged their feet in recent ranges on Tuesday with their downside supported by near-term uncertainty over the direction of the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said wariness ahead of crucial U.S. consumer confidence data due later in the day and Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony on Wednesday, deterred players from making any aggressive moves. \par \par \uc2  After a steadier start in Asia, the dollar gave in to both the yen and euro on Greenspan-related rumours and dollar selling by Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said vague rumours Greenspan would resign were not taken seriously but were used as an excuse to liquidate long dollar positions ahead of the consumer confidence data. \par \par \uc2  However, the yen-sensitive North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up most of their early gains as foreign investors in their stock markets were unimpressed by the Nasdaq's overnight gains and continued to trim recently built portfolios. \par \par \uc2  Most Southeast Asian markets had few leads to follow and moved within tight ranges in thin trade, with the exception of the Indonesian rupiah which witnessed another volatile day. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah swooned to a fresh 28-month low, marred by more than a week of ethnic slaughter in Central Kalimantan and on uncertainty over the resumption of IMF lending, before recovering some ground on aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah skidded to an early low of 9,910 as local banks and companies scrounged for dollars amid jitters about the unrest. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said state banks began selling dollars once the rupiah broke 9,900 - a level it last saw in October 1998. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was believed to be behind the selling, with the amount sold estimated at around $80 million or more. \par \par \uc2  Average daily trading volume in the onshore market has been between $50-$100 million for the past few weeks, while offshore activity has dried up following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading curbs. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah, and would hike interest rates to protect the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The one-month SBI rate now stands at 14.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  However, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  govenor Anwar Nasution reiterated that these moves would have a limited impact if Indonesia failed to get its house in order. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's latest bout of weakness comes amid fears over security as ethnic Dayaks continue their murderous rampage against Madurese settlers in the remote province of Kalimantan. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said there were also concerns over Jakarta's failure to resolve certain issues with the IMF in order to secure the release of a $400 million loan disbursal. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was testing 42.80 resistance as offshore players unwound long dollar positions ahead of the March 1 implementation of the Bank of Thailand's new disclosure rules on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  deals. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign banks both offshore and onshore were selling dollars as well as local stocks and bonds to ensure they had access to the baht after the new rules took effect. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers in Singapore said it was merely a precaution rather than a sign of real concern over the possibility of further controls. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was expected to be well-supported around 42.75/80, levels which it has not seen since February 21, as local companies were expected to buy dollars there. \par \par \uc2  But dealers added a firm break of that level could trigger stop-loss dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will issue January data on manufacturing output, exports, imports and the current account on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was trapped in a narrow range with exporter inflows limiting the downside and foreign banks, usually active on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , capping gains. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers in Manila suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , encouraged by subdued corporate demand for dollars and a steady flow from exporters, was buying dollars for foreign debt repayments. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was also nervous over the Supreme Court's closed-door hearing of a petition, filed by former president Joseph Estrada, challenging the legitimacy of President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo's administration. \par \par \uc2  Officials said the court was unlikely to rule on the petition on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the peso was likely to come under more pressure from month-end position squaring on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was virtually flat from Monday's close of 32.345 with the market reluctant to position itself ahead of Greenspan's testimony. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said trading was quiet as players ignored another piece of data showing a limping economy. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's top economic planning agency said the economy slowed in January, flashing its "blue" light for the second consecutive month. Its index of leading indicators, which forecasts peaks and troughs in the business cycle, fell 1.1 percent on month to 97.6. \par \par \uc2  It blamed the slowdown on fewer working days in January due to a week-long Lunar New Year holiday, and noted a plan to add T$111.5 billion to the 2001 budget for public infrastructure works to fuel growth. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was marginally stronger, staying well within the trading territory of the past month. \par \par \uc2  "It's nothing more than position adjustment," said one trader of Tuesday's move to the firmer end of the 1.7420-1.7480 range. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the market was squaring positions on the firmer yen, but others said it lacked clear direction. \par \par \uc2  The Sing could get that direction later in the week from the rupiah, which is teetering near the psychological 10,000 support. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a slide past 10,000 in the rupiah could weaken the Sing dollar, given Singapore's close investment ties with Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 The won gained from a firmer yen despite foreign outflows from Seoul's stock market, which ended 1.32 percent lower as foreign investors fled the futures market, leading a drop in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  But onshore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volumes were light in advance of a domestic holiday on March 1. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's going to stay quiet until the end of the week," said one trader of won non-deliverable forwards in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was likely to be long of dollars over the week, striking fresh long positions at 1,240/1,242. \par \par \uc2  Near-term dollar resistance is seen at 1,250, a level it has stayed shy of since February 19. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0831 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.13\tab  115.96\tab    -0.15\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7426\tab  1.7432\tab    +0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    32.343\tab  32.345\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1246.50\tab 1246.50\tab    +0.00\par  Baht\tab      42.84\tab   42.83\tab    -0.02\par  Peso\tab      48.15\tab   48.20\tab    +0.10\par  Rupiah\tab  9820.00\tab 9810.00\tab    -0.10\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.13\tab  114.45\tab    -1.45\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7426\tab  1.7365\tab    -0.35\par  Taiwan dlr    32.343\tab  32.900\tab    +1.72\par  Korean won   1246.50\tab 1277.00\tab    +2.45\par  Baht\tab      42.84\tab   43.70\tab    +2.01\par  Peso\tab      48.15\tab   50.75\tab    +5.40\par  Rupiah\tab  9820.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -3.56\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2r05avu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
