\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Stocks slack,  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  barely brighter. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Jennifer Chen \par \uc2 1,074 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2001\par 09:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 26 (Reuters) - Asian shares turned in a \par \par \uc2  lacklustre performance on Monday with Wall Street and talk \par \par \uc2  about rate cuts playing minor roles. Most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  steady. \par \par \uc2      Regional markets focused on growing speculation of a U.S. \par \par \uc2  rate cut before the Federal Reserve policy meeting on March 20 \par \par \uc2  given feeble equity prices and consumer confidence. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Japan was also the subject of speculation, with \par \par \uc2  dealers talking about the possibility of a return to zero \par \par \uc2  interest rates ahead of a BOJ policy meeting. \par \par \uc2      But investors were reluctant to take big positions ahead of \par \par \uc2  other key events scheduled for later in the week. The \par \par \uc2  Conference Board consumer confidence index is due out on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, and Fed chief Alan Greenspan will testify before a \par \par \uc2  Congressional committee on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      Investors also failed to find much inspiration from either \par \par \uc2  the Nasdaq's slight bounce nor a small dip in U.S. blue \par \par \uc2  chips on Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, Taiwan tech shares\tab    took a knock-on hit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Motorola's profit warning on Friday, while Korean\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shares rose slightly on the back of the rate cut\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Shares in Tokyo\tab    ended the day mixed, with techs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slipping as banking shares jumping on hopes for a BOJ easing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Hong Kong's Hang Seng\tab   was barely in negative\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par territory, but property stocks were buoyant amid the rate cut\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     RUPIAH RUFFLED, BAHT BOUNCED\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were little changed, except for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Thai baht and Indonesian rupiah , which headed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for entirely different directions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah went south as Indonesia's many economic and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political problems took their toll on local financial markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the local opening, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  quickly broke the 9,800\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level to lows not seen since October 1998 amid worsening ethnic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par violence in Central Kalimantan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said onshore trading volume was slightly higher\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than normal as the country's political and security picture\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deteriorated.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said later in the day it was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par help the battered rupiah. Senior deputy governor Anwar Nasution\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par blamed the rupiah's recent bout of weakness mainly on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bloodshed in the remote Central Kalimantan province, which has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par left up to 400 people dead in the past week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But he also added the rupiah's woes were due to a "mix of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par everything", including Jakarta's deadlock with its chief donor,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the International Monetary Fund.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Fund delayed a $400 million loan disbursement to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia because of concerns over the new regional autonomy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par laws and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  independence. Talks between the IMF and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia proved fruitless, with a new round of talks yet to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par scheduled.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In contrast, the baht took cheer from new Prime\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's plan to spend his way towards\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thaksin presented his controversial policies to parliament\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday, laying out nine top priorities to encourage economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growth that focus on consumption.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai markets were particularly pleased with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government's commitment to set up a national asset management\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par company to tackle bad debts in the system. Analysts too\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par approved of the plan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We think this is structurally positive to the market and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank shares...we are more positive on the decisiveness of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government in tackling the country's NPL problem because the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government could initiate other key policies," said Merrill\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Lynch in a research note.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINES SUSPENDS BONDS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine Bureau of Treasury said on Friday it would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par temporarily stop offering seven and 10-year Treasury bonds,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par starting this week, to bring down the government's borrowing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par costs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Both longer-dated bonds were fetching yields significantly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher than short-dated paper, with the seven-year at 16.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent and the 10-year at 17.4 percent against 10.456 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for 91-day paper and 11.783 percent for 182-day paper.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think they are just looking to fund themselves in an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par area of the curve, which is probably around the 2-5 year which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has a lower risk premium, to reduce their costs," Adam Le\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mesurier, regional economist at Goldman Sachs, told Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, Standard Chartered Bank said the Treasury can help\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prop up prices in longer-dated bonds and bring yields down only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is steadfast in maintaining low interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It is easy to see why local bond market players demanded a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher risk-premium on their investments...The BSP has a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par penchant for jacking up domestic interest rates whenever the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comes under pressure," it said in a research note.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0832 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on 