\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  says  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  to help rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2001\par 08:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Feb 26 (Reuters) - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the beleaguered rupiah and hoped to stop it breaching 10,000 against the U.S. dollar as ethnic violence in Borneo and soured relations with the IMF hit the unit. \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but we should also address the main problems, the unrest and political problems," senior deputy governor Anwar Nasution told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "Of course we hope we can stabilise the rupiah below 10,000." \par \par \uc2  By the latest trade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was being quoted at 9,840/9,860 against the dollar, lows not seen since October 1998. It closed at 9,610 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Lingering political and economic problems and sporadic bouts of violence have eaten away at the rupiah in the past year, wiping off some 25 percent of its value against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Nasution blamed its recent woes on a "mix of everything", but mainly bloodshed around the town of Sampit in Central Kalimantan province that has killed up to 400 people in the past week. \par \par \uc2  "During the past two years we have been killing each other here and now look at the Sampit issue," he said. \par \par \uc2  A spat with the IMF was also a problem, he said. \par \par \uc2  "This is also having some affect. We need a new letter of intent for restructuring external debt of the public sector under the Paris Club agreement." \par \par \uc2  Indonesia has been at loggerheads with the International Monetary Fund over a $400 million loan delayed since December due to a number of missed economic reform targets and proposed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law reforms. \par \par \uc2  Financial markets had been looking for a concrete outcome from high-level talks between Indonesia and the Fund in Washington last week but there were no breakthroughs. \par \par \uc2  The IMF on Friday described the meeting as productive, saying both sides agreed to intensify discussions but there was no hint of a fresh mission or when the loan would be released. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been relatively steady in the past month, coping well with parliament's censure of President Abdurrahman Wahid over two financial scandals and subsequent demonstrations. \par \par \uc2  Nasution said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbs announced on January 15 remained effective but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still exposed to the offshore rupiah non-deliverable forward (NDF) market. \par \par \uc2  "The rules are still effective but again that is only a very limited objective - a non underlying transaction of the rupiah, that's about it." \par \par \uc2  "We cannot ban the foreign banks in the Asian market in Singapore from doing their business. I don't even think the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Singapore can control the foreign institutions in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  units," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules introduced last month include a ban on rupiah transfers to non-residents and a lower ceiling of $3 million on cumulative forward deals onshore banks can conduct with non-residents with no underlying investment purpose. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2q057s8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoa