\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Dn Late On Corp Dlr Demand, World Bk \b0\par\par\uc2 661 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2001\par 10:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah fell 2% to its lowest level since October 1998 on strong dollar demand by corporates and banks, as international lending agencies tightened the screws on the government, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Worsening ethnic violence in Central Kalimantan province, on the island of Borneo, had also cast a shadow on the rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0900 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 9,830 rupiah, its highest level since October 1998, when Indonesia was mired in a financial crisis. Late Friday the dollar traded at IDR9,685. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah had dropped to as low as IDR9,865 earlier Monday, but found temporary respite when state banks sold dollars, probably on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and as commercial banks locked in profits, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Corporates needing to repay their foreign debts scrambled for dollars amid expectations the rupiah could weaken further, after the World Bank warned last Friday it would cease all new lending to the government if the country slips into another crisis, and amid concerns the ethnic clashes in Borneo could spread further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Participants were also wondering about the outcome of Chief Economics Minister Rizal Ramli's meeting with the International Monetary Fund last week, dealers said. There are worries about the status of the International Monetary Fund's disbursement of a $400 million loan tranche, which has been suspended since December last year, as the government and the lending agency tried to iron out differences over issues of fiscal decentralization, a controversial amendment of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, and a delayed sale of the government's stakes in two local banks. \par \par \uc2  Genuine corporate demand early in the day emerged around IDR9,725 to IDR9,775, prompting other participants to cover their short dollar positions, dealers said. This triggered stop-loss dollar buying around IDR9,800, which pushed the dollar to as high as IDR9,865, they added. \par \par \uc2  "It's an accumulation of all the bad news," said a dealer at a European bank. "Today was the turning point when everybody decided to cover their short dollar positions." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's fall Monday was its largest since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  imposed in mid-January its controversial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations, which have effectively smothered offshore trading in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers said the restrictions have only served to slow down the rupiah's descent - and not halt it - since onshore dollar demand remains strong. \par \par \uc2  "Although Bank Indonesia's restrictions have given the rupiah near-term stability, this shows the problem is not coming from the offshore market, but rather onshore," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. "BI's (Bank Indonesia) restrictions haven't helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it's aiming at the wrong target." \par \par \uc2  Deutsche Bank has advised Indonesian corporates and investors to hedge their long rupiah positions before the dollar strengthens further, said strategist Peter Redward. \par \par \uc2  As long as Indonesia's problems aren't resolved, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers said they expect the rupiah to slide further, citing the IDR10,000 as a major psychological support level. \par \par \uc2  "For the rest of this week, we'll see some pressure still on the rupiah," said the European bank dealer. "If the dollar goes to IDR10,000, it will spark panic again among the local corporate and retail players." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's fall will likely be at a more gradual pace in the short term, as participants are wary of testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Following the rupiah's fall, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials warned Monday that it was prepared to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a possible hike in the benchmark one-month Sertifikat Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday was modest, as it failed to counter the strong dollar demand, they added. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 3983 1277; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx2q00u90\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
