\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Indonesia May Raise SBI Rate To Help IDR - Anwar \b0\par\par\uc2 153 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2001\par 07:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may raise the benchmark one-month Sertifikat Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the rupiah, Senior Deputy Governor Anwar Nasution said Monday. \par \par \uc2  "We may raise interest rate again after being stable for a while," he told journalists. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's one-month SBI rate is currently at 14.75%. The rate has stabilized around that level since mid-January. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Monday, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Their statements came after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped below 9,800 rupiah to the dollar - the dollar's highest level since October 1998 - earlier Monday on local corporate dollar demand. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277;\par I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com\par -0- 26/02/01 07-16G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx2q00u3r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
