\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Domestic leads dominate as BOJ eases. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2001\par 10:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 9 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were steady to firmer late on Friday on the back of domestic leads such as asset sales and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In terms of external factors, all eyes were on the Bank of Japan's policy board meeting which stretched late into the day, intensifying speculation of an easing, especially after a local television station reported the BOJ would cut its discount rate. \par \par \uc2  This was later borne out when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its policy board decided to cut the official discount rate to 0.350 percent from 0.50 percent, effective from February 13. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time the BOJ had cut the largely symbolic rate since September 1995. It also decided by a majority decision to keep the key overnight call rate at 0.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  The yen fell to its lowest in nearly two weeks against the dollar after the discount rate cut, which the government welcomed as a move that would help boost the economy. \par \par \uc2  "The yen remained weak but regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not pay as much attention to its level as what could happen if the BOJ decides to take a decisive step to reverse this clear downtrend in the economy," said a dealer at an Asian bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "I guess people don't want to be caught too long on dollars when they return to the market on Monday. Local factors are also major drivers today," he said. \par \par \uc2  The ailing Indonesian rupiah recouped some lost ground following state bank dollar sales above 9,600, believed to be on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past several days to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Korean won ended firmer in anticipation of capital inflows after Korea Exchange Bank (KEB) announced it would soon sell its credit card unit to a foreign firm. The sale could fetch around $700 million. \par \par \uc2  Next week, investors are likely to closely watch U.S. January retail sale numbers on Tuesday and Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's bi-annual testimony before Congress on monetary policy on the same day. \par \par \uc2  The market is keen to hear the Fed chief's opinions on the economy after he told lawmakers a few weeks ago that economic growth right now was probably "close to zero." \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso ended the week on a slightly stronger note, but failed to hold onto its intraday high of 47.945 as dollar sales from exporters and overseas workers lost steam. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said exporters emerged in early trading to sell dollars that they had held since the political crisis involving former president Joseph Estrada. \par \par \uc2  They added the current stable political situation has also induced more overseas workers to repatriate their earnings. \par \par \uc2  However, the peso slipped as those sales slowed, and then dipped in reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to cut rates by 50 basis points, even though the decision was widely expected. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cut on Friday completed the unwinding of a 400 basis point hike in October to defend the peso. The overnight borrowing and lending rates will be 11 percent and 13.25 percent, respectively, from Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the bank did not expect much downside for the peso after the cuts given the calmer political situation. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said higher inflation may curb the bank's ability to ease interest rates further. January inflation rose 6.9 percent on year - the highest rate in 22 months. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won ended higher on inflow hopes after KEB said it would soon sell its credit card unit to a foreign company. \par \par \uc2  Local media said DBS Group Holdings Ltd , Citibank Corp and Standard Chartered Plc were vying for a stake in KEB Credit Card. \par \par \uc2  But the won's upside was capped by the yen's weakness, net stock sales by foreign investors, and near-term technical resistance around 1,260, the 62.8 percent retracement of the dollar/won's January 4-January 18 upmove. \par \par \uc2  On the macro front, Finance Minister Jin Nyum said Korea's growth would be reduced to below four percent in 2001 if the U.S. economy experiences a hard landing. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea has forecast that growth of 5.3 percent this year. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah edged slightly higher in thin trading, helped by state banks' dollar selling believed to be on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier in the day it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market over the past several days to help the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Violent demonstrations in East Java, the support base for beleaguered President Abdurrahman Wahid, had upset financial markets in Jakarta and placed pressure on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said local demand for dollars was sluggish, though it was expected to pick up if the rupiah strengthened past 9,580. \par \par \uc2  On the political front, Wahid delivered a fiery speech against his critics on Friday in front of his supporters in East Java. The ailing leader, who was censured by parliment over two financial scandals, was in the province to ease mounting political tensions and violence. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar nudged higher in line with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trade dominated by position squaring activities ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  "There have been lots of two-way bets on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week and people are squaring those positions because they don't know what will happen to the yen on Monday," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "Also, the market will be closely watching Greenspan on Tuesday. No one wants to be caught on the wrong side," he said. Separately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) said on Friday it did not know exactly when it would make the monetary policy statement which is eagerly awaited by the market. \par \par \uc2  The MAS said last month it was reviewing its 2001 inflation and growth forecasts given the negative external environment. \par \par \uc2  The market is divided on which way the MAS will lean. Some analysts say the top priority should be boosting growth, while others point to the need to pre-empt imported inflation. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar ended slightly higher in sluggish trade as the market continued to unwind long U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Taipei said last minute buying of U.S. dollars by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowed the local dollar's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  It has failed to convincingly test the 32.20 mark as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been consistently buying U.S. dollars throughout the week. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the bank is seeking to maintain the competitveness of Taiwan's exports, especially given the softer outlook for the yen. \par \par \uc2  The cross rate between the Taiwan dollar and yen was at 3.6140 at 0852 GMT, which some analysts said may be too high for the bank's comfort. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, though local stocks managed to gain ground on Friday on hopes over banking sector reforms, another top computer company, Acer Inc. , reported disappointing sales for January. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the week, heavyweight Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co. issued a profit warning for the first quarter of the year, underscoring the downturn in the electronics cycle. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said Taiwan is especially vulnerable to this downturn as it depends heavily on its high-tech exports. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  Onshore baht trading was light and rangebound as the market awaited key cabinet appointments from newly named Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra. \par \par \uc2  The tycoon-turned-politician, who won a January 6 election and was formally named premier on Monday, has yet to name a finance minister. \par \par \uc2  "We're still waiting to see who will be finance minister," one Bangkok baht dealer said."Right now it's tough to break through 42.30 on the downside and 42.70 on the topside." \par \par \uc2  Thaksin said the cabinet list would be finalised by February 12, but added that the finance portfolio had yet to be decided. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the baht remained in a tight range above 42.50 for most of the morning, but that some local banks and corporates had U.S. dollar sell stops above 42.60. \par \par \uc2  "If something smells bad on Monday, we could decide to break 42.70 or even 43.00," the dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0934 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.13\tab  116.22\tab    -0.78\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7462\tab  1.7460\tab    -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    32.282\tab  32.285\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1261.40\tab 1264.60\tab    +0.25\par  Baht\tab      42.62\tab   42.63\tab    +0.02\par  Peso\tab      48.01\tab   48.13\tab    +0.25\par  Rupiah\tab  9585.00\tab 9580.00\tab    -0.05\par  Ringgit\tab  3.8000\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.13\tab  114.45\tab    -2.29\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7462\tab  1.7365\tab    -0.56\par  Taiwan dlr    32.282\tab  32.900\tab    +1.91\par  Korean won   1261.40\tab 1277.00\tab    +1.24\par  Baht\tab      42.62\tab   43.70\tab    +2.53\par  Peso\tab      48.01\tab   50.75\tab    +5.71\par  Rupiah\tab  9585.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -1.20\par  Ringgit\tab  3.8000\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2906a1v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
