\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Firmer, but pitfalls remain. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2000\par 10:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 7 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were generally a touch firmer late Thursday but analysts warn the slight gains may be deceptive with many risks still lurking. \par \par \uc2  Slower U.S. growth, political uncertainty, and stalled corporate and economic reform are all affecting regional markets. \par \par \uc2  The impeachment trial of President Joseph Estrada began late Thursday in Manila, where the markets have buckled under the recent political uncertainty and signs of a flagging economy. \par \par \uc2  Thailand will hold a general election on January 6, and doubts persist over the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's president. \par \par \uc2  For the time being, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or unwinding of long dollar positions ahead of the year-end in illiquid markets will give regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a temporary boost. \par \par \uc2  The firmer yen and stronger euro also gave regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a lift. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, the market will be closely monitoring U.S. jobs data and a speech by Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Friday. Greenspan hinted at an end of monetary tightening cycle earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar spiked up to post a high of 1.7340 in late trade on what dealers said was dollar/Sing selling by some American banks. \par \par \uc2  But strong demand for the U.S. dollars from local corporates below the 1.7350 mark pulled the Sing back to around 1.7360-70, still better than its day's low of 1.7430. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers attributed the sharp move to unwinding of long U.S. dollar positions in response to Wednesday's measures by \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to encourage foreign investors to invest or issue debt in local fixed income market. \par \par \uc2  The MAS said banks could now lend to non-residents for investment in the country, saying the move would help broaden investor base for Sing dollar assets. \par \par \uc2  It also allowed banks to make transactions in Singapore dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options with other banks and financial institutions in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Sell on rumours and buy on news, that is how the market played the MAS announcement but some players might have been caught long or short," chief dealer of a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  He said the MAS announcement has disappointed those who were betting on broader liberalisation of Singapore's exchange rate policy. \par \par \uc2  Singapore manages the exchange rate against an undisclosed trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket and in the past several months has repeatedly indicated its desire of an appreciation of the Sing against that basket. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said realisation in the market was growing that the measures were positive in the long-run. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers said low trading volumes exaggerated the move. \par \par \uc2  "Remember half of the market participants are on year-end holidays so the volume is thin and that exaggerates any move," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won strengthened on exporters' dollar-selling in otherwise thin, dull trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are often exaggerated in illiquid markets, and there has been little interest in the won market with the lack of fresh incentives and year-end approaching. \par \par \uc2  As expected, the Bank of Korea kept its key overnight rate at 5.25 percent. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chon Chol-hwan said it would consider cutting interest rates when inflationary pressures ease and financial markets stabilise. \par \par \uc2  Chon also warned of an economic slowdown given shrinking exports earnings. According to Rebecca Patterson, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan, that isn't the end of the challenges Korea faces. \par \par \uc2  "The market has priced in to a degree slowdowns in both Korea and the U.S. But we have more room to go. This isn't over, in Korea we're going to get more restructuring hiccups, more labour union strikes, and confidence, if you look at consumer or business surveys, is tanking," she said. \par \par \uc2  JP Morgan recently revised its won forecast to 1,270 by the end of the first quarter next year. \par \par \uc2  Patterson also noted that given a more competitve export sector, Korean authorities are also keeping a close eye on the yen/won cross-rate, seeking a range of 10.25-11.50. It stood at 10.81 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was steady in late trade despite a rash of bad news for the island's economy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign-equity related inflows and exporters boosted the local dollar. But analysts have said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will weaken as economic growth slows. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's November trade surplus came in far below expectations, falling 45.6 percent on year to US$774.6 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  later said it expected full year 2000 exports to grow slower than previously expected due to a global economic slowdown. \par \par \uc2  The data comes on the heels of a revision of Standard & Poor's outlook for Taiwan to negative from stable because of delayed economic reforms as the political impasse between the president and legislature drags on. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dipped in November to US$108.231 billion due to an increase in private foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits. Analysts said bank's defence of the local dollar might also have had something to do with the fall. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht shuffled towards the higher end of a narrow 43.49-43.65 range in line with firmer regionals. \par \par \uc2  But dealers in Bangkok said volumes were negligible, with only a few local corporates and banks in the market. Offshore players continue to shy away from the baht market following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's clampdown on speculation. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts expect the baht to see further weakness in the run-up to the election and in its aftermath. \par \par \uc2  "The new government will likely be even weaker than the current. You have an economy that is slowing, reforms that are going slowly, and yields which are still low," JP Morgan's Patterson said. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was helped up, after it hit a day low of 9,635, by state-run banks which dealers said were active on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It was basically the state banks...yes they were selling dollars on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They were selling dollars all along from 9,620 to 9,570," said chief dealer of a U.S. bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  He said some dollar supply, close to rupiah's lows, was also seen coming from exporters. \par \par \uc2  Talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent Jakarta-based foreign banks and Singapore-based players scrambling to unwind their long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said importers and local corporates took advantage of the easing dollar and came in to support the dollar at around 9,550 level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said as soon as the market senses lack of state banks' support, the rupiah would be back beyond the 9,600 level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was closely watching developments surrounding the controversial revamping of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said the Parliament that would go into recess from Saturday has yet to approve proposed changes in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws aimed at making the bank more accountable and empower government to sack the institution's top officials. \par \par \uc2  The proposed changes have come under criticism as an attempt to bring under government control an institution that is guaranteed wide-ranging independence under existing laws. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor on Wednesday resumed control of his office after nearly six months detention on charges of corruption. \par \par \uc2  Sjahril Sabirin's release from house arrest and his return to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised fears of fresh rift between President Addurrahman Wahid and the bank. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's chief economics minister Rizal Ramli said on Thursday changes to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws are expected to be approved by the parliament in January or February. \par \par \uc2  He also said all members of the board of governors should resign when the changes stand approved. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso edged down in late trade but moved in a tight range through most of the day with most players stayed away from the market as the impeachment trial against President Joseph Estrada began. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the other factor that kept players cautious was Friday's weekly meeting of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary board. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hinted earlier in the week of a cut in excessively high key domestic interest rates to help boost weakening economic growth. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a cut in rates was widely expected, after a 50 basis point cut earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  "But the uncertainty is on how deep the cut will be. So people are taking a cautious view," a dealer at a European bank in Manila said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  taking advantage of a relatively quite day was buying dollars to replenish its reserves. \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     110.27\tab  110.87\tab    +0.54\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7330\tab  1.7407\tab    +0.44\par  Taiwan dlr    33.038\tab  33.065\tab    +0.08\par  Korean won   1194.00\tab 1198.20\tab    +0.35\par  Baht\tab      43.38\tab   43.60\tab    +0.51\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   50.00\tab    +0.00\par  Rupiah\tab  9570.00\tab 9517.00\tab    -0.55\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     110.27\tab  102.21\tab    -7.31\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7330\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.98\par  Taiwan dlr    33.038\tab  31.380\tab    -5.02\par  Korean won   1194.00\tab 1135.00\tab    -4.94\par  Baht\tab      43.38\tab   37.45\tab   -13.67\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   40.20\tab   -19.60\par  Rupiah\tab  9570.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -27.12\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwc70ajok\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picsc