\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Higher On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2000\par 11:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed slightly higher Friday after a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but dollar demand remains healthy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar nudged to IDR9,565 in intraday trade, just short of its year-high of IDR9,580, but Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it lower. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at IDR9,520, down from IDR9,535 late Thursday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar-demand is still strong as corporates seek the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to service yearend debts. \par \par \uc2  New figures showing Indonesia's November consumer price index was higher than expected, up 9.12% on-year and 1.32% on-month due to higher food prices, didn't impact the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was also unmoved by data showing imports rising 68.3% on-year in October, causing the trade surplus to decrease to $2.03 billion. \par \par \uc2  Traders said market players are still worried about the International Monetary Fund's concerns over the economy. \par \par \uc2  In a strongly worded letter dated Nov. 8, Anoop Singh, the Fund's Washington-based deputy director for Asia and the Pacific, demanded Jakarta move swiftly to reduce risks in its fiscal decentralization plan, use higher oil revenues to repay government debt and set a firm timetable for asset sales. \par \par \uc2  Failure to do so by early December, the letter suggests, could stop the IMF's board from approving fresh loans to the country under its $5 billion bailout program. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's interbank overnight rate continued to hover around 10.75% to 10.85% - little changed from the previous day - as liquidity in the system remains sufficient. \par \par \uc2  -By Leigh Murray, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; leigh.murray@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwc105qv7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
