\par\par \b \uc2  Jakarta says  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  can still support rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2000\par 06:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 21 (Reuters) - Indonesia's chief economics minister Rizal Ramli said on Tuesday Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  can still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the ailing rupiah despite the resignations from its board of governors. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Ramli said: "They remain active until new members (are appointed). They still have the right to make decisions." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was trading at 9,450/9,470 against the dollar at 0455 GMT. It has lost more than 20 percent against the dollar this year, making it one of Asia's worst performers. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its acting chief and the six other deputy governors would quit to make way for a management reshuffle and a recapitalisation. \par \par \uc2  But the future of two deputy governors who did not sign the resignation letter and a third who did but was not included in the government's formal notification to parliament remains unclear. \par \par \uc2  Announcing the resignations, Bank Indonesia said the officials would continue their duties until replacements are named. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbl01dfq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
