\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mixed on U.S. unease, steady euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2000\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a mixed \par \par \uc2  bag late Friday as uncertainty on the U.S. elections dragged on \par \par \uc2  and lack of fresh leads on local factors kept market activity \par \par \uc2  subdued. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Euro's\tab   Wednesday gains against the dollar helped by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and U.S. election turmoil,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also made players cautious on their long dollar positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against some of the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Most regionals moved in a tight range and some were helped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by authorities or by the fear of their action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Reluctance on part of players to hold on to long dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions through the weekend given lack of fresh leads\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par signalling direction of the markets or mood of the authorities,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also helped.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso, however, lived up to its reputation of being\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relatively the most volatile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region and amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , moved both ways.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won and the Taiwan dollar were seen more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par disturbed by the second day of losses on the tech-heavy Nasdaq\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but unabated foreign fund inflows into equity markets helped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keep sentiment positive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro in early European trade held close to its day's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peak around $0.8685 on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wariness, while the yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par came under pressure after downgrade of official estimates of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Japan's economy for the first time in two years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht rose to a high of 43.36 in low volume trade amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par what dealers said was a lull in demand for dollars from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates and on lack of activity by offshore players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said upticks in the Sing, rupiah and peso also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par helped sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Most orders placed in the past week or ten days have been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par filled. So there is not much demand for the dollars in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market and the regionals are also doing fine today," a dealer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at a European bank in Bangkok said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dealer said baht was also supported by a steadier local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity market that had seen foreign fund inflows earlier in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said dollar/baht was seen supported at around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 43.15-43.20 levels, from where the dollar had rebounded last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week and in mid-October.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Sing dollar clung to a tight range, with few factors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pushing it either way.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A dealer at a European bank said there was some local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate demand for U.S. dollars around 1.7350 and 1.7380. He\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par added that those companies were probably hoping to buy U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar during the Sing dollar's recent run-up, and missed out\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on those lower rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A stronger yen and euro is keeping the Sing dollar away\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from falling much past 1.7400. The local dollar is managed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against a trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Looking ahead, dealers said third-quarter economic growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data due out next Friday was not likely to influence the local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar's direction. However, the European bank dealer added he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected the Sing dollar to fall past the 1.7500 level if the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data proves to be very strong, but still fails to boost the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah moved in a narrow range and was close to its day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high of 9,210 in late trade helped by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and on lack of fresh leads.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  acting governor Anwar Nasution confirmed the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost the troubled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said it will continue to do so.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The battered rupiah has lost over 20 percent this year,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par making it one of Asia's worst performers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It seems the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wants to hold the 9,200-9,250\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range and it has been able to do that in the past couple of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par days because there is very little demand from the corporates or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from offshore players," a dealer at a U.S. bank in Jakarta\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Positive movement of the Sing and the baht also helped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment, the dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said a relatively calmer political front has also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cooled down the volatile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won crept towards the lower end of the day's range with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par caution dominating trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Korea's corporate reforms had cheered the market, pushing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the won to around 1,131 won. But dollar-buying by a state bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par triggered fears that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While foreign equity-related inflows have lifted the won in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent sessions, analysts are still pointing to souring\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par external factors as dimming the outlook for the won. Lower chip\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prices and a slowdown in the U.S. economy will hurt Korea's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par export-dependent economy, and some analysts forecast the won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakening towards the 1,150 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar eased back towards Thursday's closing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par levels after a hectic day of trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After propelling past the 32 level thanks to leftover\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-related inflows, the Taiwan dollar then lost ground on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fund outflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said they suspected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par help the Taiwan dollar, and that it also bought U.S. dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier to cap the Taiwan dollar's rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Morgan Stanley Capital International's re-weighting of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan's stocks has helped fuel the Taiwan dollar's gains in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent sessions. However, analysts are divided on whether the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par effect of the re-weighting significantly changes the outlook\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the local dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some argue that the re-weighting signals massive foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows and will power the Taiwan dollar higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Others, such as UBS Warburg, argue Taiwan's fundamentals\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are weakening, and that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is concerned about\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slower economic growth in Taiwan as well as the entire region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It said in a research note that only if the Taiwan dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par breaks 31.50 would it change its view that the bank is willing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to allow a weaker Taiwan dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso slipped in late trade, after touching a day high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 49.25, on rumours amid vague concerns that the banking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par industry may be in trouble.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rumours were later denied by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rafael Buenaventura who said the country's banking sector was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par healthy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The governor also said he received text messages on his\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mobile phone about two Philippine banks encountering financial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par difficulties.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's not true," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The onshore market closed at 50.20 to the dollar, from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday's close of 49.95.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso stayed up for most of the day on talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  presence in the market and on inflow of some remittances\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from overseas workers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There were rumours about some local banks ...and that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pulled down the peso very sharply," a dealer at a European bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Manila said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dealer said the market jittered by the continuing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political struggle between President Joseph Estrada and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par opposition has turned very volatile and susceptible to rumours.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Estrada is facing growing pressure to step down amid an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par impeachment trial on allegations he accepted bribes from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gambling syndicates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pumped in at least $15 million in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par morning session and a couple of banks offloaded remittance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows estimated at around $20 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Total volume for the day $166 million, compared to $185.8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     107.66\tab  107.28\tab    -0.35\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7390\tab  1.7403\tab    +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr    32.062\tab  32.065\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1134.00\tab 1132.30\tab    -0.15\par  Baht\tab      43.53\tab   43.59\tab    +0.14\par  Peso\tab      50.10\tab   49.80\tab    -0.60\par  Rupiah\tab  9220.00\tab 9250.00\tab    +0.33\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     107.66\tab  102.21\tab    -5.06\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7390\tab  1.6640\tab    -4.31\par  Taiwan dlr    32.062\tab  31.380\tab    -2.13\par  Korean won   1134.00\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.09\par  Baht\tab      43.53\tab   37.45\tab   -13.97\par  Peso\tab      50.10\tab   40.20\tab   -19.76\par  Rupiah\tab  9220.00\tab 6975.0