\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  To Use Rate Hike,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Help IDR \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2000\par 05:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - - 07/11/04-59G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0459GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  - - 07/11/05-07G \par \par \uc2  0507GMT \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia acting governor Anwar Nasution repeated Tuesday that the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue raising interest rates and sell the dollar in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the sagging rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "We will utilize all mechanisms including interest rate hike, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and stepping up on-site inspection on banks (dollar-rupiah transactions)," Nasution told reporters. \par \par \uc2  He expects that the moves will bring the dollar down to IDR8,500 at the end of the month. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 9.215 rupiah at 0527 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Nasution reiterated that Bank Indonesia hasn't made any decision whether it will lower the maximum amount, from its current $5 million, of rupiah that banks can sell to non-Indonesian residents in forward transactions. \par \par \uc2  "We have to study the advantages and disadvantages of such policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  He added that cutting down the limit may hurt banks in Singapore, which are active participants of the dollar-rupiah trading. \par \par \uc2  This is something that Indonesia doesn't want as "Singaporean banks contribute a lot to the Indonesian economy," he said. \par \par \uc2  Nasution also brushed aside a suggestion to make exporters compulsorily repatriate their dollar revenues to Indonesia to help the rupiah. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Farida Husna;Dow Jones Newswires;62-21 3983 1277\par -0- 07/11/00 05-42G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the International Monetary Fund's deputy director for Asia\par and Pacific, Anoop Singh, said that any change that Bank Indonesia may\par consider will be "consistent with the current exchange rate system."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He didn't comment on whether the IMF will approve the move to cut the\par forward limit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government adopts a floating exchange rate system and an open\par capital account regime, which doesn't place any restriction on the\par transfer of funds in and out of the country. All fund flows, however,\par must be reported to bank Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singh added that the rupiah's current weakness is beyond economic\par fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Farida Husna;Dow Jones Newswires;62-21 3983 1277\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwb705clp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
