\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  says to continue rupiah  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 156 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2000\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the embattled rupiah and that recent interest rate hikes were not sufficient to help. \par \par \uc2  Asked by reporters whether the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and would continue to do so, acting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Anwar Nasution said: "This week, last week, next week." \par \par \uc2  He said increases of several basis points in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark SBI rates - which has been the trend in recent weeks - was not enough to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "Several basis points are not yet big enough," Nasution said on the sidelines of a debt conference. \par \par \uc2  Nasution added that he firmly believed the rupiah should be stronger than 9,000 to the dollar. At 0300 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 9,138/9,158. It has come under fresh pressure in the past few days. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb202p72\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
