\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Higher On Nasdaq Boost \b0\par\par\uc2  By Arran Scott \par \uc2 948 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2000\par 10:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closed stronger in Asia\par Wednesday, after an overnight rebound in the Nasdaq dispelled some of\par the gloom plaguing the region while signs emerged that South Korea\par might be making progress in restructuring its economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar, however, ended lower Wednesday amid outflows of foreign equity funds from the local market, traders noted. \par \par \uc2  A holiday in the Philippines - where political turmoil has hurt sentiment in the region as a whole in recent weeks - also contributed to the respite in markets Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won was swept higher as stock prices in Seoul soared in response to the Nasdaq's 5.6% overnight jump and signs that the government might be getting out of the business of propping up teetering companies - which could be a positive development for the economy in the long run. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah also got a break from its recent battering amid signs of easing pressure on the embattled President Abdurrahman Wahid. The U.S. dollar slid to 9,150 rupiah Wednesday, down from a three-month high of IDR9,490 earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  But bargain hunters, betting that lingering political uncertainty in Indonesia will continue to plague its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helped to put a floor under the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar and the Thai baht were lifted in part by buoyant rupiah and won. However, a new rule in Thailand that kicked in Wednesday requiring traders to report the purpose of each \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transaction stifled trading in the baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the U.S. dollar at S$1.7498, easing from S$1.7563 late Tuesday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 43.630 baht, down from THB43.885 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors piled into Korean shares Wednesday - boosting the won in the process - on reports that the government and creditors of Hyundai Engineering & Construction Co., one of the country's biggest construction companies, are considering the option of court receivership for the troubled construction company. \par \par \uc2  Market players took that to be a clear sign that the government won't try to prop up the troubled company - an indication that progress might be made in stripping the excess from South Korea's economy. \par \par \uc2  Hyundai Engineering narrowly avoided bankruptcy Tuesday following a debt default Monday. It faces more default risks because it's still having difficulty in securing loan extensions. \par \par \uc2  Late Wednesday, the U.S. dollar was at 1136.0 won, down from KRW1139.70 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The won got a boost from the stock market," said Steve Brice, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  However, Brice said that while the many people rejoiced at signs that South Korea is moving ahead with restructuring, the market still has to take account of the fallout from such moves - higher unemployment and other negatives that could weigh on the economy going forward. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The cyclical element will still have to be priced in," Brice said.\par - - 01/11/00 09-18G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar bucked the general trend Wednesday, falling against\par its U.S. counterpart. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  supported the\par Taiwan dollar during thin early trading, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eventually\par succumbed to weakness in local stock prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan's main stock index Wednesday closed down 119.16 points at\par 5425.02.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In addition to restructuring hopes, the won also found support from\par data showing South Korea recorded a wider-than-expected trade surplus in\par October, dealers said. The surplus stood at $1.4 billion in October,\par wider than a consensus estimate of $1.2 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Insofar as the Nasdaq's rally overnight helped to precipitate a\par rebound in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the region remains vulnerable to another\par shock from U.S. stock markets, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That is because not much has changed in terms of politics - the major\par factor recently driving down most regional markets and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Nasdaq's rise is "positive in the short-term, but it's clear that\par a lot of issues remain as far as domestic politics are concerned,"\par Standard Chartered Bank's Brice said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said political turmoil in the Philippines is far from over.\par And that spells bad news for the peso, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso could come under renewed downward pressure if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't take remedial measures at its Monetary Board meeting this\par Friday, a dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Indonesia, Vice President Megawati Sukarnoputri's call Tuesday for\par Indonesian Democratic Party of Struggle members to stand behind Wahid\par helped bandage market sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That helped drag the U.S. dollar down against the rupiah and has some\par traders pondering whether the dollar will fall back below IDR9,000. The\par dollar had traded in a tight IDR8,800-IDR8,980 range for more than a\par month until this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian officials were quick to play up the rupiah's rally, telling\par the market that easing political tensions - not the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - were\par behind the move.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There was no government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  behind the rupiah's rebound\par today," \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Senior Economics Minister Rizal Ramli said. He\par attributed the rupiah's strength to Megawati's decision to increase\par support for Wahid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, traders said the political situation in Indonesia remains\par precarious and tensions could flare up again if a serious candidate for\par president emerges to challenge Wahid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That has some people thinking that the rupiah might not have far to go\par before it slides again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The rupiah's rally looks pretty much exhausted," Brice said, adding\par he expects support to emerge around IDR9,050-IDR9,100.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Arran Scott, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par arran.scott@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwb1059a2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
