\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 's Ramli denies rupiah  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2000\par 08:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's chief economics minister Rizal Ramli on Wednesday denied saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week to prop up the battered rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Ramli also said the rupiah's gains earlier on Wednesday were due to a better political climate after comments from some politicians that they supported embattled President Abdurrahman Wahid. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, Ramli told reporters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There was no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Ramli said on Wednesday, when asked to reconfirm that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spent $10 million last week to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some analysts had said the amount was too small to affect the market. \par \par \uc2  Ramli on Tuesday blamed the rupiah's sharp fall the previous day on politicians who had demanded Wahid step down. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers say Bank Indonesia usually spends between $5-10 million daily in what \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials say is aimed at smoothing fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 9,145/9,165 against the dollar in afternoon trade on Wednesday compared with 9,330/9,380 in late trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Average daily turnover on the dollar/rupiah market is about $200 million, far lower than the more than $1 billion daily before the Asian financial meltdown hit in mid-1997. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb102wqq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
