\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Indonesia Spent $10 Million Last Wk To Stabilize Rupiah -Min \b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2000\par 09:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank Indonesia spent $10 million last week to stabilize the rupiah, Senior Economics Minister Rizal Ramli said Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Last week almost $10 million was the cost for stabilizing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Rizal told reporters, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will spend more this week to help the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Rizal's comments come after President Abdurrahman Wahid said Monday he was concerned by rupiah weakness, but didn't think the government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to a low of IDR9,490 Tuesday after Wahid's remarks, which confused the market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently followed a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah when it drops through IDR9,000. \par \par \uc2  Players moved to sell dollars on Rizal's comments, pushing the pair to IDR9,350, down from 9,400 before the news. \par \par \uc2  Rizal didn't specify how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize the rupiah, but Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally uses a combination of selling dollars through state banks, and drawing down its supply of foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277;\par tom.wright@dowjones.com\par -0- 31/10/00 08-31G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwav058v2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
