\par\par \b \uc2  Central Bk Watch: Bk Indonesia Helped By Politics \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Wright \par \uc2 793 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2000\par 02:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Indonesia's cloudy political picture ironically offers the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  a window of opportunity to support the rupiah more effectively than it has been able to do in past, some economists say. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, a relatively peaceful meeting of coalition leaders in Yogyakarta, central Java, helped to ease fears that President Abdurrahman Wahid could be impeached by a meeting of the nation's highest legislative body next week. \par \par \uc2  But the gathering failed to reassure investors that Wahid's political opponents won't make such a move later this year, ensuring that political concerns will linger over Jakarta for months to come. \par \par \uc2  While damaging for investor confidence, the lack of clarity also discourages players from taking large positions for or against the rupiah in the forward market. And with fewer players in the market, Bank Indonesia should be better able to prop up the ailing rupiah by selling dollars to prevent any sharp moves. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with some effectiveness at the moment\par given that the market is so thin," says Simon Flint, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist at Bank of America in Singapore.\par -\par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  After 21-Month Dlr High\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After rising to a 21-month high against the rupiah in mid-July, the\par dollar has fallen back following \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Acting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, Anwar Nasution, has also backed up the\par dollar selling with comments that Bank Indonesia is acting in tandem\par with Singapore and other foreign monetary authorities to curb\par speculation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Apart from the fear of getting caught long dollars in such an illiquid\par market, foreign banks are also being very careful not to anger the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Indonesia has put officials in many of the foreign dealing rooms,\par ostensibly to check banks are keeping to regulations governing maximum\par forward positions, but also to apply moral pressure not to speculate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  resorted to this kind of moral persuasion without\par success last month, after a series of interest rate hikes were unable to\par stem a hemorrhage of foreign capital from Indonesia due to political\par concerns.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rate hikes to 13.53% on the one-month note at last week's auction did\par little to help the rupiah amid growing opposition to Wahid's\par ten-month-old administration, and the arrest of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor,\par Sjahril Sabirin, amid allegations of corruption.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In such an environment, direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , backed up by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par relatively small $27 billion gross foreign reserves, was ineffective.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But with thinner market conditions prevailing now, dollar selling from\par state banks is having an impact, pushing some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategists to advise investors to get rid of any outstanding\par long-dollar positions on spikes in the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again to keep the rupiah stable in the\par run up to the MPR," says UBS Warburg Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Mansoor\par Mohi-uddin.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Thus with the offshore market still long dollar and Bank Indonesia\par holding approximately $7 billion worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, the dollar\par should be sold on rallies above IDR9,000 as we head toward the MPR," he\par adds.\par -\par         Political Pressure Not Over\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Longer term, strategists' views on the rupiah depends on how they see\par the political situation unfolding.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Many analysts, including Bank of America's Flint, see the rupiah\par moving back through IDR8,500 to the dollar if Wahid survives the MPR,\par from IDR8,933 at Tuesday's close of Asian trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Flint points out that the Yogyakarta meeting, although positive,\par won't stop Wahid's political opponents from piling on the pressure later\par this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Any concerted political effort against Wahid could easily change\par investor sentiment, and make central \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less effective.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If there is a major shift in political risk, then it won't be\par effective," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par UBS Warburg's Mohi-uddin is also targeting IDR8,500 in the short-term\par on the likelihood of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But like Flint, he points out that politicians such as Amien Rais,\par head of the MPR, have said Wahid could face impeachment later in the\par year, which would hurt rupiah sentiment, and leave the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par helpless.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although the MPR has no constitutional power to impeach Wahid at this\par month's meeting, the 700-member body will consider legislation that\par could allow them to call the president to a special session later this\par year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That session would have the power to impeach the president.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This could make markets worry about impeachment even if Wahid\par survives this month," Mohi-uddin said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Added to creeping U.S. interest rates, rupiah gains might only be\par short-lived, he adds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277;\par tom.wright@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1184 4253 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw8203s8c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
