\par\par \b \uc2  MAS offers no comment on Bank Indonesia support. \b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2000\par 12:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 21 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) declined comment on Friday on whether Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had asked it to help stop offshore speculation in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  MAS said it was Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It is Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision whether to stabilise the rupiah or take appropriate actions, including inspecting foreign banks in Indonesia," a MAS spokesman said in a written reply to Reuters queries. \par \par \uc2  MAS said it was official policy not to comment on its dealings with other central banks, other banks' actions or their exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's acting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Anwar Nasution, said earlier on Friday the bank had asked neighbouring countries, such as Singapore, to help stop offshore speculation in the rupiah in a bid to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "They also see the need for the rupiah to stabilise because of their huge interest in Indonesia," Nasution said. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also confirmed it had sent inspectors to monitor local banks' trading of the rupiah and said it had the right to continue such inspections in the future. \par \par \uc2  The move had been seen as an attempt by Bank Indonesia to curb speculation in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The dollar lost almost six percent against the rupiah during the week amid the moves by Bank Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  ((Singapore Newsroom, (65) 870-3080; Fax: (65) 776-8112, singapore.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7l01d05\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
