\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 4-Bombs rattle rupiah, threaten Indonesia economy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrew Marshall \par \uc2 712 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2000\par 11:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 5 (Reuters) - Indonesia's increasingly hostile political atmosphere rained further damage on the frail economy on Wednesday as the rupiah was swept to 16-month lows on fears of worsening instability and interest rates were hiked to defend it. \par \par \uc2  A bomb blast at the attorney-general's office late on Tuesday shattered windows and blew doors off their hinges. The damage done to Indonesia's hopes of economic recovery was worse. \par \par \uc2  The blast spurred jittery offshore players to mark down the rupiah, kicking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through technical support at 8,970 to the dollar and psychological support at 9,000, and sparking a clamour for dollars from panicked local corporates. \par \par \uc2  The discovery of more explosives at the attorney-general's offices on Wednesday dealt another blow to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sending it to 9,305/9,335 to the dollar by 0845 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is now at its weakest levels since March 1999, when fears were rife that upcoming parliamentary and presidential elections would descend into mass bloodshed and instability. \par \par \uc2  When Abdurrahman Wahid became president in October after a remarkably peaceful transition to democracy, it was hailed as a milestone on Indonesia's road to recovery. The fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market now judges political risk to be as severe as in the uncertain days of early 1999 shows how badly things have gone wrong. \par \par \uc2  POLITICAL UNCERTAINTY, ECONOMIC PAIN \par \par \uc2  The explosion at the attorney-general's office came amid swirling controversy over reports that several legislators would be questioned for stirring up trouble in the unruly country. \par \par \uc2  Wahid also faces a showdown with parliament next week, after legislators exercised their right to summon him for the first time ever, to explain the controversial sacking of two ministers. \par \par \uc2  The president must also navigate a meeting of the country's highest legislative body, the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR), in August. The MPR has the power to remove him, although analysts believe this is unlikely and his main potential rivals have said they will continue to give him their support. \par \par \uc2  But while Wahid is unlikely to be toppled, his grip on power looks increasingly tenuous, and with political risk rising most foreign investors are simply turning their back on the country. \par \par \uc2  The floundering rupiah, moreover, threatens to snuff out one of Indonesia's few bright spots - a relatively strong consumer-led economic recovery after two years of pain. \par \par \uc2  A weaker rupiah makes the debt burden crushing both the government and private sector even heavier. It threatens to re-ignite inflation. And by forcing interest rates up, it makes the huge bill of bank recapitalisation even higher. \par \par \uc2  "It's fair to say the rupiah is the foundation for everything," said the head of treasury at a European bank in Jakarta. "If it goes, everything else starts to go." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is now trading far from the level of 7,000 to the dollar assumed in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current budget. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  LITTLE USE \par \par \uc2  Reports that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave the rupiah some respite on Wednesday, but dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not work for long, something the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also conceded. \par \par \uc2  "About \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we will not sell dollars because it will not help... At the moment, the problem is different, therefore monetary policy needs to be implemented consistently," Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Miranda Goeltom told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's weekly auction raised the benchmark SBI one-month interest rate to 12.69 percent from 12.33, the ninth consecutive rise in the rate, which now stands at its highest levels since December, further burdening businesses and pushing up government interest payments on bank recapitalisation bonds. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say that if interest rates stay this high for much longer, the cost of bank recapitalisation will start biting even harder into the government's budget. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was a pattern to the action in the rupiah, with onshore corporates which need dollars for debt repayments and imports holding off, hoping for better levels to buy. But when key levels are broken, they panic and pile in. \par \par \uc2  "Generally volumes are still very low, you just get bursts of activity and that's what happened this morning," said Steve Brice, treasury economist at Standard Chartered in Singapore. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7502fua\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
