\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah off lows as Wahid tries to defuse tension. \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2000\par 11:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 4 (Reuters) - The battered Indonesian rupiah was off its day lows on Tuesday as worries over political uncertainty eased after President Abdurrahman Wahid attempted to defuse a potential showdown with parliament. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has flirted with 9,000 to the U.S. dollar in the past two days on concerns over Indonesia's political stability. \par \par \uc2  By 0845 GMT it was being quoted at 8,948/8,963, after earlier coming close to 9,000, hitting its lowest levels since March 1999. It was quoted at 8,910/8,930 in late local trade on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Some liquidation of long dollar positions following Wahid's remarks capped the rupiah's fall and provided it with solid support at around 8,960, but the outlook remains fragile," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was likely to be well supported at around 8,975 and immediate resistance was seen at around 8,900. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was likely to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the market, albeit in small amounts, to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engaged in minor \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the battered rupiah, acting Bank Indonesia head Anwar Nasution said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Nasution repeated comments he made last week that the rupiah would become more stable after a key meeting in August of the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR), which will hear an account of President Abdurrahman Wahid's first turbulent year in office. \par \par \uc2  Offshore players, particularly European and British players, had bought dollars at around 8,900 earlier in the day but liquidated their long dollar positions in late trade, one bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Wahid denied on Tuesday saying parliamentarians were "culprits" behind violence in the country, and he lashed out at unnamed parties for playing political games. \par \par \uc2  In comments that appear to be an attempt to defuse a potential showdown with parliament, Wahid told a news conference that some legislators would only be questioned as witnesses over the country's troubles. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Bambang Sudibyo said on Tuesday the rupiah's fair value against the dollar, based on the country's economic fundamentals, was between 6,500 to 7,500. ((Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw7402ccb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
