\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Ends Flat; Sjahril Effect Short-Lived \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2000\par 12:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended Asian trade flat Monday after moving higher in the late afternoon following comments by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin pledging that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the local unit. \par \par \uc2  Sjahril told reporters the bank will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market "every day" to support the rupiah, which authorities have repeatedly stressed in recent weeks is undervalued given the improving economy. \par \par \uc2  The governor's comments pushed the dollar to an intraday low just below 8,600 rupiah, but continuing concerns over the Indonesian political situation pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to end at IDR8,608, flat from Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  "If nothing special happens on Tuesday I think we'll see a higher U.S. dollar," said a foreign bank trader in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Last month, Sjahril said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it would prove effective. \par \par \uc2  The dollar should trade in an IDR8,600 to IDR8,670 range Tuesday, traders said. At the lower end of the band, local importers are eager to buy dollars, the foreign bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  Among factors hurting the rupiah are concerns that an uncertain political climate is slowing the pace of debt restructuring. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's major tool to help the rupiah, which has lost 18% since January, is to push up local rates through its weekly auction of Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes. \par \par \uc2  But traders said rates on the one-month notes would have to rise significantly from around 11.13% in recent auctions to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. \par \par \uc2  With the banking system still on its knees due to huge problem loans, the government won't be keen to raise rates much higher, the foreign bank trader added. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; tom.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6c02vpi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
