\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Focus On Won \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2000\par 11:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed against the dollar in late regional trade Monday. \par \par \uc2  But a rise in the yen late in the session to Y106.60 from an intraday low of Y107.20 helped all the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  close well above their lows for the day. \par \par \uc2  The won ended domestic trade higher against the dollar at 1,113.4 from Friday's close of KRW1,114.4 as foreign investors sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay for recent purchases on the local bourse. \par \par \uc2  The Korea Composite Stock Price Index, or Kospi, rose 1.1% Monday to 845.81, and is up 16% so far this month. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors sold about $350 million for won in the Seoul \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday, traders said. Foreigners also remained net buyers on the Korea Stock Exchange, purchasing a net KRW157.9 billion in shares during the session. \par \par \uc2  However, dollar purchases by state-run institutions including Korea Development Bank, Korea Electric Power Corp. and Korea Asset Management Corp. limited its decline. \par \par \uc2  After a one day delay, North and South Korea are expected to begin their historic first-ever summit Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said any movements in local stocks on news emanating from the talks likely will affect the won. The meeting was delayed by one day at the request of North Korea. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar is unchanged from late Friday at 39.065 Thai baht and at 8,615 Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the rupiah by selling dollars. \par \par \uc2  "If necessary, we are going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market every day," Sjahril told reporters ahead of an appearance before a parliamentary committee on the Bank Bali case. \par \par \uc2  Sjahril, however, declined to say the amount of dollars the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to sell to boost the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  His comments helped the rupiah recover from an intraday low of IDR8,650, although traders doubted the move would generate any sustainable rise unless the political climate improves. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has weakened 18% since early January. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a touch weaker against its Singapore counterpart at S$1.7235 from S$1.7257 previously. \par \par \uc2  Traders say a number of European institutions are keen to buy the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on any weakness toward S$1.7300 to pay for purchases of Singapore stocks, which closed a touch higher. \par \par \uc2  Philippine markets were closed Monday for a national holiday. The dollar ended last week at 42.465 pesos. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended trade in Taipei at NT$30.802, up from NT$30.786 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  -By Benjamin Pedley; 65-421-4485; ben.pedley@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw6c02vns\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
