\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia rupiah buoyed by capital controls talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2000\par 11:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, June 2 (Reuters) - The rupiah was off its intraday highs by late trade on Friday but was still well supported by speculation Indonesia may introduce some form of capital controls in a bid to prop up the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said he was opposed to outright capital controls but would be willing to discuss with the government "grey area" measures such as steps to control the flow of the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Trade and Industry Minister Luhut Pandjaitan said the idea of capital controls was still being studied, and added that he thought the current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime was too liberal. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime is too free, so it needs adjustment," Pandjaitan said. \par \par \uc2  By 0900 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 8,463/8,493 to the dollar, versus 8,640/8,670 in late trade on Wednesday. Jakarta markets were closed on Thursday for a holiday, but the rupiah managed to briefly breach 8,400 in thin offshore trade. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ignored bullish April trade data, as well as inflation data from May which was in line with expectations. \par \par \uc2  "It's talk about capital controls that is driving the market," said a dealer at a European bank in Jakarta. "People are suddenly worried about being short of rupiah." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said onshore players actively covered short rupiah positions shortly after the local market open on Friday, boosting the rupiah to a high of 8,410 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But they said talk of capital controls remained speculative and may not boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for long. \par \par \uc2  "Many players remain uncertain on what kinds of capital controls the government might be considering. One of the options may be to force the repatriation of exporters earnings back into the country but this is easier said than done," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with CNN, Sabirin said the rupiah was undervalued. \par \par \uc2  "On an economic basis I still believe the rupiah should be around 7,000 and perhaps maybe a bit stronger than 7,000," Sabirin said. \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rupiah would depend on the volatility of the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "If there is in our view any use for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we do so. But of course we do not want to waste our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that may not be beneficial for the medium-term stability of the curency," he told CNN. ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw62049p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
