\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Indonesia may consider curbs on rupiah flows. \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2000\par 04:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 2 (Reuters) - Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin said on Friday he was opposed to outright capital controls but would be willing to discuss with the government "grey area" measures such as steps to control the flow of the beleaguered rupiah . \par \par \uc2  In a brief telephone interview with CNN from Jakarta, monitored in Tokyo, Sabirin said he believed the rupiah on economic grounds was worth at least 7,000 to the U.S. dollar - more than 17 percent above current levels. \par \par \uc2  "I don't really believe in capital controls for Indonesia but in some grey areas, for example limiting the flow of rupiah and so on..., we may discuss whether or not there is a benefit from that," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said. \par \par \uc2  Speculation Indonesia might be on the verge of imposing capital controls gathered momentum on Thursday, aided in part by a comment by the new managing director of the International Monetary Fund, Horst Koehler, that capital controls were not a taboo. \par \par \uc2  But speaking in Bangkok, Koehler said they should be introduced only under special circumstances. \par \par \uc2  Koehler is due to meet Indonesian President Abdurrahman Wahid later on his Asian tour. \par \par \uc2  Frustration with the economic policies of the Wahid administration, especially its perceived failure to accelerate the pace of corporate and legal reforms needed to boost investor confidence, has contributed to a recent slide in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Fresh outbreaks of religious and ethnic violence across the sprawling archipelago have also soured sentiment toward the rupiah, which briefly breached the 8,400 to the dollar level on Thursday before falling back to to around 8,450. \par \par \uc2  It was quoted near 8,500 in early Asian trading on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "On an economic basis I still believe the rupiah should be around 7,000 and perhaps maybe a bit stronger than 7,000," Sabirin said. \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rupiah would depend on the volatility of the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "If there is in our view any use for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we do so. But of course we do not want to waste our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that may not be beneficial for the medium-term stability of the curency," he told CNN. \par \par \uc2  ((Alan Wheatley, Asian Economics Correspondent, Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432-8453 email: alan.wheatley@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw62042m5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
