\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Indonesia may consider curbs on rupiah flows. \b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2000\par 07:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, June 2 (Reuters) - Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin said on Friday he was against outright capital controls but would be willing to consider "grey area" measures such as steps to control the flow of the beleaguered rupiah. \par \par \uc2  In a brief telephone interview with CNN from Jakarta, Sabirin said he believed the rupiah on economic grounds was worth at least 7,000 to the U.S. dollar - more than 17 percent firmer than current levels. \par \par \uc2  "I don't really believe in capital controls for Indonesia but in some grey areas, for example limiting the flow of rupiah and so on..., we may discuss whether or not there is a benefit from that," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said. \par \par \uc2  Trade and Industry Minister Luhut Pandjaitan said later on Friday that the idea of capital controls was still being studied, but added he thought the current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime was too liberal. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime is too free, so it needs adjustment," Pandjaitan said, adding that this would not harm the economy. \par \par \uc2  "The risk is very small, and in order to stabilise the rupiah I don't see any worry about that," he said. \par \par \uc2  RUPIAH LIFTED BY CONTROLS TALK \par \par \uc2  Speculation Indonesia might be on the verge of imposing capital controls has boosted the rupiah, aided in part by a comment in Bangkok on Thursday by the new managing director of the International Monetary Fund, Horst Koehler, that capital controls were not a taboo. \par \par \uc2  Koehler is due to meet Indonesian President Abdurrahman Wahid later on his Asian tour. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 8,485/8,505 to the dollar at 0500 GMT, compared with 8,640/8,670 in late Jakarta trade on Wednesday. Indonesian markets were closed on Thursday for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market remained unsure on the likelihood of capital controls and what form they would take. \par \par \uc2  "Many players remain uncertain on what kinds of capital controls the government might be considering. One of the options may be to force the repatriation of exporters' earnings back into the country but this is easier said than done," one said. \par \par \uc2  FRUSTRATIONS WITH POLICIES \par \par \uc2  Frustration with the economic policies of the Wahid administration, especially its perceived failure to accelerate the pace of corporate and legal reforms needed to boost investor confidence, has contributed to a recent slide in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Fresh outbreaks of religious and ethnic violence across the sprawling archipelago have also soured sentiment toward the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "On an economic basis I still believe the rupiah should be around 7,000 and perhaps maybe a bit stronger than 7,000," Sabirin said. \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rupiah would depend on the volatility of the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "If there is in our view any use for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we do so. But of course we do not want to waste our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that may not be beneficial for the medium-term stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he told CNN. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6203yvm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
