\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Indonesia Gov: Interest Rate Rise Wed Due To Weak IDR \b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2000\par 12:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank Indonesia may have to revise its key macroeconomic forecasts if the rupiah remains weak, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a news conference after meeting parliamentary leaders, Sjahril also said that the increase in interest rates at Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  note auction was an inevitable result of the rupiah's weakness. \par \par \uc2  "This is something that cannot be avoided, this is a result of the weakening rupiah," Sjahril said. \par \par \uc2  He added however, that he doesn't expect interest rates to continue to rising. \par \par \uc2  Interest rates on one-month Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes jumped four basis points at Wednesday's auction, as yields continued to creep up in the wake of a rate hike in the U.S. and amid the lingering weak rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the rate increase was an apparent attempt by Bank Indonesia to shore up the flagging rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Sjahril said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was preparing a "pessimistic scenario to face some bad conditions," for all of its key forecasts, including inflation, growth and interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "Now, Bank Indonesia is making preparations in order to revise assumptions, if conditions remain unstable," Sjahril said, although he stressed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't yet revised any of its forecasts. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia forecasts growth this year of between 3% and 4% and inflation of between 5% and 7%, if the government presses ahead with budgeted fuel price increases. \par \par \uc2  Higher interest rates put direct pressure on the state budget and guiding rates up is something the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is clearly reluctant to do. \par \par \uc2  The government has issued IDR309 trillion worth of bonds as of April to recapitalize 25 local banks and is expected to issue a further IDR100 trillion of bonds to recapitalize several state and private banks. \par \par \uc2  The bonds carry fixed and floating rates tied to the average interest rate of Bank Indonesia's three-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes, which currently stands at 10.91%. \par \par \uc2  The government calculates the cost to the budget this year of interest payments on the bonds of 6.5% of gross domestic product. As well as increasing the pressure on Indonesia's recovering economy, hiking rates now would jack up this already massive bond interest payment bill. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah slipped to a seven-month low of IDR8,768 May 12. Although it has since recovered some ground - it ended Asian trade at IDR8,505 Wednesday - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains weak and well off the IDR7,000 to the dollar level on which the 2000 budget is based. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia says the rupiah's weakness is due to political factors, rather than economic issues. It has also sent mixed signals as to whether it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom said earlier that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, although she reaffirmed that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  changes dollars into rupiah on the market as required. \par \par \uc2  Sjahril said he doesn't expect interest rates to continue on an upward trajectory. \par \par \uc2  "I expect the weak rupiah won't be for too long, so interest rates won't keep on increasing," he said. \par \par \uc2  The upward trend in U.S. interest rates has also put Indonesian yields under pressure. Sjahril said he didn't know whether another hike in the U.S. in July would put more pressure on Indonesian rates. \par \par \uc2  "We'll see how the situation is in the market," Sjahril said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't want to risk raising interest rates. \par \par \uc2  -By Grainne McCarthy; 62 21 3983 1277; gmccarthy@ap.org \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5o02kfv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
