\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Rules Out More Rupiah Support \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2000\par 08:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank Indonesia Governor Sjahril Sabirin said Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no plans to further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "Only if needed, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market; if not (needed) we don't want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Sjahril told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "It takes time to strengthen (the) rupiah because it must be done gradually and depends on the market sentiment." \par \par \uc2  His comments come after he said Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold less than $300 million to boost the rupiah in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this week. \par \par \uc2  He said Bank Indonesia had spent less than 1% of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but didn't offer more details. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia said that the country's gross international reserves as of May 5, which are net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves plus outstanding \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts, were at $29.478 billion. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah slumped to a seven-month low last Friday as volatility returned to haunt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a mix of factors that included the expected tightening bias by the Federal Reserve, slow domestic economic reforms and a barrage of confusing comments by senior policymakers. \par \par \uc2  At 0614 GMT, the dollar was trading at IDR8,418, compared with IDR8,350 late Wednesday. The market was closed Thursday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  -By Leigh Murray 62 21 3983 1277; leigh.murray@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5j02gms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
