\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah boosted by news on IMF letter of intent. \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2000\par 05:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, May 17 (Reuters) - News that the Indonesian government would sign a delayed letter of intent with the International Monetary Fund later on Wednesday boosted sentiment on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  By 0300 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 8,475/8,500 to the dollar compared with 8,545/8,595 in early trade before the news and 8,500/8,550 in late local trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The positive news boosted sentiment on the rupiah. But the upside for the local unit seems to be limited as higher corporate dollar demand emerged at around the 8,450 area," one bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The signing of the letter of intent was necessary to release a $400 million loan originally due in April. The IMF delayed release of the loan because of the government's slowness in moving on reforms. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said lingering concerns about President Abdurrahman Wahid's handling of the economy were also likely to limit the rupiah's upside. \par \par \uc2  A decision by the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise borrowing costs by 50 basis points, as expected, its biggest move in five years, surprised no one but helped remove one of the uncertainties hanging over the rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The 50 basis-point hike does help remove one of the negative factors. But concerns remain on the government's poor handling of the economy. Now it no longer has significant external factors to blame," one dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was slow as state banks, which led dollar selling on Tuesday after Wahid asked them to do so, were not yet active in the market in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Wahid on Tuesday asked Bank Indonesia and state banks to help the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which had fallen more than 18 percent against the dollar so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers questioned whether \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could bring a sustainable recovery in the rupiah - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already said it does not regard \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or interest rate hikes as a viable solution as political factors play a large part in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Wahid, facing a growing crisis of confidence in his handling of the economy, also ordered his finance minister to review economic projections in this year's budget which are now looking too optimistic. ((Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5h00e7d\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (indonesia near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertal